      <data key="k493">The essay stresses that a repository rarely captures the full behavior of a legacy service: contracts, migrations, user journeys and institutional knowledge remain external. Small reversible changes, context gathering and reproducible tests are offered as controls against locally successful but architecturally wrong agent patches.</data>
