      <data key="k493">The essay contrasts "light" factories that retain human interpretation with "dark" factories that minimize review, exposing the trade-off between throughput and lost comprehension. Osmani argues that harness capability and measurable verification should determine safe autonomy, not the attraction of unattended execution.</data>
