      <data key="k198">A</data>
      <data key="k199">W192 is a data-resource study, not independent validation of a two-axis autonomy framework; W152 is a better research-roadmap comparator.; The original essay explicitly introduces two dimensions (agency and orchestration) and six levels; the earlier one-dimensional paraphrase dropped the framework.; Represent the genuine two-axis framework and its six levels rather than reducing it to a generic risk-tier recommendation.; Capture the two axes, scope of six levels, and lack of empirical validation.; Agency vs orchestration is best represented through execution, human-agent delegation and escalation.; Do not promote conceptual taxonomy or market hypotheses into established research outcomes.</data>
