      <data key="k484">O010</data>
      <data key="k493">Osmani argues that a one-dimensional autonomy ladder hides the difference between what one agent may do and the ability to coordinate many agents. He proposes two axes—agency and orchestration—and six practical levels: assist, supervised action, scoped task delegation, goal-driven autonomy, parallel delegation, and managed-by-exception orchestration. Risk, reversibility, independent checks and escalation limit the appropriate level for any task.</data>
      <data key="k505">https://addyo.substack.com/p/agentic-autonomy-levels</data>
      <data key="k520">2026</data>
    </node>
