      <data key="k493">Osmani argues that engineering decisions should start with user needs and observable benefit rather than technical elegance. He offers questions to ask before development, during iterative implementation and after launch, supported by practices such as support-ticket analysis, behavioral observation, interviews and product feedback. The article does not evaluate AI coding systems.</data>
