      <data key="k260">Voluntary replies across Bluesky, X and Threads; early-adopter self-selection. Canonical newsletter body and chart report 155 responses (77+62+16); one blog sentence says 145. Use 155 only as the canonical author-reported count, not an independently verified sample. The public blog supplies the IDE portion, not the complete newsletter, which also contains industry-news material. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
      <data key="k267">The poll describes early-adopter preferences, not industry market share or measured productivity. A conflicting 145-response sentence in the blog is retained as a source-edition discrepancy.</data>
      <data key="k268">Editor preference and adoption belong to workflow evidence, not causal productivity estimates or benchmarked capability.</data>
