      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Gergely Orosz","category":null,"collection":"P","id":"P040","kind":"practitioner_article","label":"Stack overflow is almost dead","limitation":"Updated 19 May 2025. The causal contribution of LLMs is not identified by the time series. This non-Pulse-titled blog article is an excerpt of a Pulse issue originally published 2025-05-15. It passes the literal title-prefix rule; it is excluded by the optional stricter Pulse-origin filter. The parent issue is provenance only, not another P article. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.","mapped":["C:C09","C:C10"],"printed":false,"streams":["T:System knowledge &amp; memory","T:Skills &amp; learning"],"summary":"Updates an earlier analysis of falling Stack Overflow question counts, considering moderation history, alternative communities and LLM-based assistance.","topics":["K:System understanding and rationale","K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"],"url":"https://blog.pragmaticengineer.com/stack-overflow-is-almost-dead/","volumes":[],"year":"2025-05-15"}</data>
      <data key="k127">Use credited authors and contributor roles as recorded; publication curation does not make Orosz the original author of all guest/excerpted material.</data>
      <data key="k128">Gergely Orosz</data>
