      <data key="k237">Updates an earlier analysis of falling Stack Overflow question counts, considering moderation history, alternative communities and LLM-based assistance.</data>
      <data key="k246">practitioner_article</data>
      <data key="k248">Stack overflow is almost dead</data>
      <data key="k260">Updated 19 May 2025. The causal contribution of LLMs is not identified by the time series. This non-Pulse-titled blog article is an excerpt of a Pulse issue originally published 2025-05-15. It passes the literal title-prefix rule; it is excluded by the optional stricter Pulse-origin filter. The parent issue is provenance only, not another P article. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
      <data key="k267">The observations concern new questions, not all site usage or knowledge value. The headline and shutdown forecast go beyond what the descriptive series demonstrates.</data>
      <data key="k268">The follow-up concerns knowledge-community activity; fewer questions do not prove disappearance of all usage or knowledge value.</data>
