      <data key="k246">practitioner_article</data>
      <data key="k248">Cursor makes developers less effective?</data>
      <data key="k260">P052 says 136 issues and implies assignment by developer. METR’s primary methodology reports 246 issues and issue-level randomization, with developers working in both conditions. Do not reproduce the secondary account’s conflicting design description. A primary abstract/methodology check was performed, not a full-paper audit or statistical replication. This is a retitled Pulse excerpt; preserve its existing series provenance. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
      <data key="k267">The primary study reports slower completion in this specific early-2025 setting. P052’s broader all-tools inference and proposed familiarity explanation remain interpretations; neither is independent causal validation.</data>
      <data key="k268">This is secondary commentary on W023, not a replication; the all-tools extrapolation and causal learning-curve explanation are unsupported.</data>
