      <data key="k248">What is “loop engineering?”</data>
      <data key="k260">P110 directly links https://addyosmani.com/blog/loop-engineering/ (7 June 2026). O012 catalogues the substantially matching Substack edition (8 June 2026). Treat the edge as discussion of the same underlying work via an alternate edition, not an exact-URL citation. The paid remainder and comparative loop outcomes remain unreviewed. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
      <data key="k267">The article questions whether custom loops remain useful as harnesses absorb them. Context design, bounded scope and measurable benefit are more defensible than assuming that more looping improves results.</data>
      <data key="k268">The critique challenges unnecessary custom orchestration, not the need for bounded execution, context and independent assurance.</data>
