      <data key="k260">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
      <data key="k292">["%  Sources: Spec Kit's clarification template; GSD's CLARIFY_BEFORE_PLAN rule.]", "\\paragraph{Practical example.} Tuesday at 10:14 Marta runs \\code{sdd new feat-042} followed by \\code{sdd run @clarification feat-042}. The agent returns seven questions: two P1 (``what is the PKCE \\code{code\\_verifier} lifetime?'' and ``does revocation cascade to issued ID tokens?''), four P2 (rate-limit ceiling, redirect-URI allow-list, log-retention horizon, device binding policy), one P3 (preferred clock source for token \\code{nbf}). Gate~1 stays closed until the security PO answers the two P1s; the four P2 assumptions are recorded in \\code{clarifications.md}. Gate~1 opens at 14:30, with the spec measurably less ambiguous than the version Marta would have shipped to \\code{@architect} unaided."]</data>
      <data key="k373">PAT:067</data>
      <data key="k460">124</data>
      <data key="k463">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter15_patterns.tex</data>
      <data key="k467">91</data>
