      <data key="k260">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
      <data key="k292">["\\textbf{Ralph connection:} This is exactly the Planning Mode vs.\\ Building Mode distinction from \\chapref{ch:ralph}. Huntley's approach of using separate prompts for planning and building is an instance of this pattern. The key insight from the pattern catalogue is that the \\textit{plan itself should be treated as disposable}—regeneration is cheap, salvaging a corrupted plan is expensive."]</data>
