      <data key="k260">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
      <data key="k292">["\\textbf{Ralph connection:} This maps to Huntley's observation that Ralph ``works best as a technique for bootstrapping Greenfield, with the expectation you'll get 90\\% done with it.'' The dual-agent pattern formalizes the transition point: when do you switch from aggressive generation to careful maintenance? The answer is usually when your test suite is robust enough to serve as backpressure."]</data>
