    <node id="OCC:AGENT:17">
      <data key="k107">Blast Radius Containment</data>
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"practices","collection":null,"families":["FAMILY:F06"],"id":"OCC:AGENT:17","kind":"practice_occurrence","label":"Blast Radius Containment","limitation":"Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Historical occurrence of Blast Radius Containment in the retained V04 source. The original title, alias and file locator preserve its lineage. Read PAT:017 for the current English operational guidance and its qualifications.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V04"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k162">OCC</data>
      <data key="k212">F06</data>
      <data key="k213">Security of the Toolchain and Its Effects</data>
      <data key="k246">practice_occurrence</data>
      <data key="k248">Blast Radius Containment</data>
      <data key="k250">en</data>
      <data key="k260">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
      <data key="k292">["\\textbf{Solution:} Contain the agent's ``blast radius'' through layered isolation: sandboxed execution environments (Docker, E2B), minimal credential exposure (only necessary API keys), network isolation (egress restrictions), and resource limits (CPU, memory, disk).", "\\textbf{Ralph connection:} This is the sandboxing strategy from \\chapref{ch:safety} formalized as a pattern. The pattern catalogue adds a structured approach: enumerate all resources the agent can access, then systematically restrict each to the minimum required. Huntley's philosophy—``It's not if it gets popped, it's when. And what is the blast radius?''—is the pattern's guiding principle."]</data>
      <data key="k373">PAT:017</data>
      <data key="k460">317</data>
      <data key="k463">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter09_patterns.tex</data>
      <data key="k467">310</data>
      <data key="k477">3c88f9e5d7b0288e46de69503668ac80ecb7778165d80bf74eab10da30c4e2ba</data>
      <data key="k487">HISTORICAL_SOURCE_OCCURRENCE</data>
      <data key="k513">V04</data>
    </node>
