    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0056">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0056","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Cotroneo and colleagues \\autocite{W039} compare human and generated code across defect, vulnerability and complexity measures, while Improta and colleagues \\aut","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Cotroneo and colleagues \autocite{W039} compare human and generated code across defect, vulnerability and complexity measures, while Improta and colleagues \aut</data>
      <data key="k263">15</data>
      <data key="k265">15</data>
      <data key="k306">Cotroneo and colleagues \autocite{W039} compare human and generated code across defect, vulnerability and complexity measures, while Improta and colleagues \autocite{W052} expand the comparison through paired function generation and language-specific analysis. The studies\textquotesingle{} abstracts describe different profiles of findings, not a single scalar score. In particular, \workposs{W039} ISSRE 2025 version of record studies more than 500,000 code samples in Python and Java. \workposs{W052} September 2026 preprint reports 787,562 function pairs spanning Python, Java and C. The latter generates candidate functions from human docstrings; that design provides a controlled comparison but does not reproduce every contextual constraint of an existing repository.</data>
      <data key="k446">4bbac99818a79fe3f94b2b89d9ae3fffbce30e0ed4fdbfeb11b77963c93eb93c</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W039", "W052"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0057">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0057","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The unit of comparison becomes even more important once we look at the actual methods. Cynthia, Muttakin and Roy \\autocite{W029} start with the AIDev curated su","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The unit of comparison becomes even more important once we look at the actual methods. Cynthia, Muttakin and Roy \autocite{W029} start with the AIDev curated su</data>
      <data key="k263">25</data>
      <data key="k265">25</data>
      <data key="k306">The unit of comparison becomes even more important once we look at the actual methods. Cynthia, Muttakin and Roy \autocite{W029} start with the AIDev curated subset of 33,596 agentic pull requests, select 8,106 bug-fix PRs, restrict them to 1,802 Python PRs in 206 projects, and finally analyze 1,210 that were merged. Their SonarQube procedure compares a base commit with its merged successor and records newly introduced static-analysis issues. This is a post-merge code-quality snapshot, not a longitudinal study of subsequent human repair or observed outages. The narrowing of the sample is part of the finding\textquotesingle s meaning: it does not describe rejected PRs, non-Python code, or all kinds of agentic work (\autocite{W029}, PDF pp.~1--2, Methodology and Table 1).</data>
      <data key="k446">bc1a9508ebfaf0b85953ccf6df5ab4c956d475fe8e118bca52554c0d69bee23a</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W029"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0058">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0058","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Kraishan \\autocite{W054} asks a different question. The September 2026 preprint draws 37,623 labeled PRs from AIDev and a human comparison group in the same 2,8","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Kraishan \autocite{W054} asks a different question. The September 2026 preprint draws 37,623 labeled PRs from AIDev and a human comparison group in the same 2,8</data>
      <data key="k263">27</data>
      <data key="k265">27</data>
      <data key="k306">Kraishan \autocite{W054} asks a different question. The September 2026 preprint draws 37,623 labeled PRs from AIDev and a human comparison group in the same 2,807 repositories. It joins additional GitHub responses and follows a subset of 26,283 merged PRs for 90 days. Its maintenance proxies include changed-file follow-up activity and detected reverts; they do not identify every subsequent modification as a repair of an original defect. The paper explicitly acknowledges that the most-changed file is a proxy for whole-PR churn, revert detection can miss silent rewrites, and agents were not randomly assigned to tasks (\autocite{W054}, PDF pp.~2, 5, 7). These are different measurements, not rival answers to one identical experiment.</data>
      <data key="k446">fc3716b69db3c5f0e0c92347e19a4519f122b2f8df4b99dc3726cdca2d17c26f</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W054"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0059">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0059","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The apparent tension between \\autocite{W039} and \\autocite{W052} is instructive. \\autocite{W039} reports that generated code is generally simpler and more repet","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The apparent tension between \autocite{W039} and \autocite{W052} is instructive. \autocite{W039} reports that generated code is generally simpler and more repet</data>
      <data key="k263">31</data>
      <data key="k265">31</data>
      <data key="k306">The apparent tension between \autocite{W039} and \autocite{W052} is instructive. \autocite{W039} reports that generated code is generally simpler and more repetitive in its sampled Python and Java programs, alongside high-risk security findings. \autocite{W052} reports that AI functions can be shorter and less branching while displaying language-dependent security patterns; in its comparison, size-adjusted complexity carries less discriminating signal. Neither result implies that an AI-authored feature is automatically more maintainable than a human-authored one. Both rely on the precise definitions of a defect warning, a vulnerability category and a complexity statistic.</data>
      <data key="k446">24df33255a67f10ab1cbf82b64c359911304800d429257a75c1aeb459dcb4120</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W039", "W052"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0060">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0060","kind":"cited_passage","label":"He and colleagues' Cursor adoption study \\autocite{W004} uses observable committed configuration files to assign treatment, a proxy that may miss private or unc","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">He and colleagues' Cursor adoption study \autocite{W004} uses observable committed configuration files to assign treatment, a proxy that may miss private or unc</data>
      <data key="k263">43</data>
      <data key="k265">43</data>
      <data key="k306">He and colleagues' Cursor adoption study \autocite{W004} uses observable committed configuration files to assign treatment, a proxy that may miss private or uncommitted adoption. Liu and colleagues \autocite{W055} examine technical debt in generated code. Agarwal and colleagues \autocite{W001} study later agent adoption in AIDev v3 repositories, stratified by prior IDE use. The W001 and W004 studies share investigators and related analytical techniques, and should be treated as related observational evidence rather than statistically independent validations; one study's percentage must not be substituted for the other's. \autocite{W001,W004}</data>
      <data key="k446">82b779f7b39767dd0d804d8a000526066b5b932288c06a2f52dc837b8d60b768</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W001", "W004", "W055"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0061">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0061","kind":"cited_passage","label":"An agent that sees only the function it is asked to modify may create a new helper rather than discover a reusable service already present elsewhere. The result","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">An agent that sees only the function it is asked to modify may create a new helper rather than discover a reusable service already present elsewhere. The result</data>
      <data key="k263">49</data>
      <data key="k265">49</data>
      <data key="k306">An agent that sees only the function it is asked to modify may create a new helper rather than discover a reusable service already present elsewhere. The resulting patch can be locally sensible and globally redundant. Huang and colleagues \autocite{W031} report that AI-generated pull requests in their sample often overlook reuse opportunities, producing more redundancy even while reviewer sentiment may be neutral or positive. Wu\textquotesingle s clone research \autocite{W044} supplies a complementary topic, but its original manuscript has not yet been independently inspected for this chapter.</data>
      <data key="k446">271326211861e2a07720326e094ddfed006a35ebf4271a395330df71dd949785</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W031", "W044"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0062">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0062","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Zhu, Tsantalis and Rigby \\autocite{W059} examine code and architecture smells in LLM- and agent-driven development. Their preprint describes structural degradat","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Zhu, Tsantalis and Rigby \autocite{W059} examine code and architecture smells in LLM- and agent-driven development. Their preprint describes structural degradat</data>
      <data key="k263">63</data>
      <data key="k265">63</data>
      <data key="k306">Zhu, Tsantalis and Rigby \autocite{W059} examine code and architecture smells in LLM- and agent-driven development. Their preprint describes structural degradation in the studied systems, but its strongest language about general laws should be treated as the authors\textquotesingle{} interpretation until the full methods and statistical results are inspected. Huang\textquotesingle s reuse findings \autocite{W031} provide a narrower observation. Historical ownership work such as Greiler \autocite{W175} helps frame responsibility and stewardship; it does not prove that a particular module layout is correct.</data>
      <data key="k446">748a626e36b8db9803bb25ef3032885e44b9f9802ee580899eff94a16b447300</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W031", "W059", "W175"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0063">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0063","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Kraishan\\textquotesingle s churn analysis \\autocite{W054} uses a proxy based on the most-changed file and normalizes by PR size. Its conclusion that none of the","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Kraishan\textquotesingle s churn analysis \autocite{W054} uses a proxy based on the most-changed file and normalizes by PR size. Its conclusion that none of the</data>
      <data key="k263">77</data>
      <data key="k265">77</data>
      <data key="k306">Kraishan\textquotesingle s churn analysis \autocite{W054} uses a proxy based on the most-changed file and normalizes by PR size. Its conclusion that none of the five agents imposes a measurably higher per-line maintenance burden in the observed window is therefore conditional on the measure, coverage, window and selection criteria. It does not contradict \workposs{W029} finding that merged bug-fix PRs can introduce static-analysis issues. Both observations can hold simultaneously. A code smell introduced at merge need not produce a later edit within ninety days, and later maintenance may arise for reasons unrelated to an original smell.</data>
      <data key="k446">418b80e8970819f7aed79764bcc678db31e79ecd9901092fd9fc211d7ac43ce3</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W029", "W054"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0064">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0064","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The studies discussed above follow different parts of maintenance. Cynthia and colleagues examine issues introduced by agent-generated changes, while Kraishan f","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The studies discussed above follow different parts of maintenance. Cynthia and colleagues examine issues introduced by agent-generated changes, while Kraishan f</data>
      <data key="k263">83</data>
      <data key="k265">83</data>
      <data key="k306">The studies discussed above follow different parts of maintenance. Cynthia and colleagues examine issues introduced by agent-generated changes, while Kraishan follows subsequent file activity; Watanabe and colleagues study agentic pull requests more broadly. Their results require the version, denominator and follow-up window recorded in Appendix~\ref{app:methodology}. The targeted manuscript checks already performed do not amount to complete reanalysis of every source. \autocite{W029,W054,W036}</data>
      <data key="k446">758528515959c1dbea336f79c130dc81868109c1232a68862d0552a41fbcd05e</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W029", "W036", "W054"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0065">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0065","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The studies\\textquotesingle{} denominators also explain why apparently conflicting vendor stories should not be averaged. \\autocite{W029} analyzes only merged P","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The studies\textquotesingle{} denominators also explain why apparently conflicting vendor stories should not be averaged. \autocite{W029} analyzes only merged P</data>
      <data key="k263">101</data>
      <data key="k265">101</data>
      <data key="k306">The studies\textquotesingle{} denominators also explain why apparently conflicting vendor stories should not be averaged. \autocite{W029} analyzes only merged Python bug-fix PRs and has no human baseline. \autocite{W054} includes multiple languages and a matched human comparison from the same repositories, then further narrows its longitudinal sample to PRs with a full 90-day observation window. \autocite{W036} follows 567 Claude Code PRs across 157 projects and reports that 83.8\% were merged, with 54.9\% of merged PRs integrated without further modification. Its manual task-purpose classification covers 213 agentic and 221 human PRs, with multiple labels allowed; it is not a randomized comparison of agent quality (\autocite{W036}, PDF pp.~1, 6--7).</data>
      <data key="k446">2a91a2b5959bcfa337d497c7f828ff2ff24d0be1dccbf11d9a2d7ec21a4d66b6</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W029", "W036", "W054"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0066">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0066","kind":"cited_passage","label":"AIDev underlies both \\autocite{W029} and \\autocite{W054}. Their overlapping provenance means that agreement between them should not be counted as independent re","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">AIDev underlies both \autocite{W029} and \autocite{W054}. Their overlapping provenance means that agreement between them should not be counted as independent re</data>
      <data key="k263">103</data>
      <data key="k265">103</data>
      <data key="k306">AIDev underlies both \autocite{W029} and \autocite{W054}. Their overlapping provenance means that agreement between them should not be counted as independent replication, even though they construct different subsets and measure different endpoints. A future synthesis could stratify by task type, language, patch size and repository, but the published aggregate tables alone are insufficient to perform that meta-analysis responsibly.</data>
      <data key="k446">ed36bf7030e9ad427f50b670d328d1fbc371136933cca47b458867f2bfa643f6</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W029", "W054"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0067">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0067","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Kraishan\\textquotesingle s cross-agent maintenance study \\autocite{W054}, Pinna\\textquotesingle s task-stratified acceptance analysis \\autocite{W034}, and Mazlo","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Kraishan\textquotesingle s cross-agent maintenance study \autocite{W054}, Pinna\textquotesingle s task-stratified acceptance analysis \autocite{W034}, and Mazlo</data>
      <data key="k263">107</data>
      <data key="k265">107</data>
      <data key="k306">Kraishan\textquotesingle s cross-agent maintenance study \autocite{W054}, Pinna\textquotesingle s task-stratified acceptance analysis \autocite{W034}, and Mazloomzadeh\textquotesingle s agentic-PR research \autocite{W057} point to the need for contextual comparisons. Their shared repositories or agent datasets must be checked before treating results as independent corroboration. A model\textquotesingle s capability score, an agent\textquotesingle s merge rate and the subsequent maintenance cost of its changes are different estimands.</data>
      <data key="k446">963df6cd14d70ee253157f9857f2d95a7f025d511255bab44e455070e3f253f0</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W034", "W054", "W057"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0068">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0068","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Bird and colleagues \\autocite{W182} examine associations between ownership and software quality in historical projects. Wheeler\\textquotesingle s \\textquotesing","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Bird and colleagues \autocite{W182} examine associations between ownership and software quality in historical projects. Wheeler\textquotesingle s \textquotesing</data>
      <data key="k263">115</data>
      <data key="k265">115</data>
      <data key="k306">Bird and colleagues \autocite{W182} examine associations between ownership and software quality in historical projects. Wheeler\textquotesingle s \textquotesingle substrate collapse\textquotesingle{} argument \autocite{W189} challenges the continued validity of authorship-derived knowledge metrics under AI generation. These are different evidence classes: one is empirical background on ownership, while the other proposes a conceptual diagnosis of changing authorship signals. Xu\textquotesingle s newcomer-participation research \autocite{W058} is a useful boundary because participation and stewardship are not the same outcome.</data>
      <data key="k446">23c5406f26ea5d2301a122230c385edbe2b257bd0dac9bb44251126bbd0d9a4e</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W058", "W182", "W189"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0069">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0069","kind":"cited_passage","label":"\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth,height=.62\\textheight,keepaspectratio]{figures/jpg/13_Figure_5_1_Architect.jpg}\n\\caption{How post-merge quality is measured. C","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
