    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0098">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0098","kind":"cited_passage","label":"\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth,height=.62\\textheight,keepaspectratio]{figures/jpg/18_Figure_7_2_Architect.jpg}\n\\caption{Reliability grows through an evidence","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">\includegraphics[width=\linewidth,height=.62\textheight,keepaspectratio]{figures/jpg/18_Figure_7_2_Architect.jpg}
\caption{Reliability grows through an evidence</data>
      <data key="k263">31</data>
      <data key="k265">27</data>
      <data key="k306">\includegraphics[width=\linewidth,height=.62\textheight,keepaspectratio]{figures/jpg/18_Figure_7_2_Architect.jpg}
\caption{Reliability grows through an evidence-gate ladder. Conceptual redraw of W095, original Figure 2; \workref{W095}. Original author presents a synthesis framework, not an empirically validated universal standard. A benchmark pass supplies evidence for one gate, not production acceptance.}
\label{fig:ch07-research-2}
\end{figure}
</data>
      <data key="k446">46e80266b37d2ebb9307b747eb9f1ee78ef43c345f47567af43e11b05f2a9ce9</data>
      <data key="k463">figures/source_redraws/figure_ch07_02.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W095"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0099">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0099","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The difference between code activity and delivery, introduced through Demirer and colleagues \\autocite{W010}, explains why local coding gains need not become re","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The difference between code activity and delivery, introduced through Demirer and colleagues \autocite{W010}, explains why local coding gains need not become re</data>
      <data key="k263">15</data>
      <data key="k265">15</data>
      <data key="k306">The difference between code activity and delivery, introduced through Demirer and colleagues \autocite{W010}, explains why local coding gains need not become release gains. Research on review effort and AI-generated changes (\autocite{W063}, \autocite{W094}) addresses a different part of that chain: reviewers must reconstruct intention, understand a diff and assess the strength of its checks. A study measuring the number of comments cannot by itself measure whether those comments prevented defects. Nor does faster review imply a better decision if reviewers overlook the very risks that justify review.</data>
      <data key="k446">87157904e76592696d28893a074031f6d71f981fca0c0bd027da29cb2ec8e894</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W010", "W063", "W094"]</data>
