    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0100">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0100","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Khojah et al.~\\autocite{W069} use eye tracking and interviews in a Wizard-of-Oz review experiment. Their primary abstract reports that LLM provenance labeling i","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Khojah et al.~\autocite{W069} use eye tracking and interviews in a Wizard-of-Oz review experiment. Their primary abstract reports that LLM provenance labeling i</data>
      <data key="k263">31</data>
      <data key="k265">31</data>
      <data key="k306">Khojah et al.~\autocite{W069} use eye tracking and interviews in a Wizard-of-Oz review experiment. Their primary abstract reports that LLM provenance labeling increased fixation time without changing the measured thoroughness of review. This observation cautions against equating attention, elapsed time, trust or accuracy. Its full participant-level methods and effect estimates still need examination before stronger numerical claims can be made.</data>
      <data key="k446">5bf5c2559dfec1e81f0968fd61ae4211b6059d3cc4c40353825497e892ec965e</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W069"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0101">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0101","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Studies of review complexity \\autocite{W073}, developer perceptions \\autocite{W069} and review outcomes \\autocite{W088} motivate separating patch size from cogn","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Studies of review complexity \autocite{W073}, developer perceptions \autocite{W069} and review outcomes \autocite{W088} motivate separating patch size from cogn</data>
      <data key="k263">35</data>
      <data key="k265">35</data>
      <data key="k306">Studies of review complexity \autocite{W073}, developer perceptions \autocite{W069} and review outcomes \autocite{W088} motivate separating patch size from cognitive difficulty. Their detailed coefficients remain subject to original manuscript verification. The engineering point is that provenance is a clue about how a change was produced, not a verdict about its correctness. A human-authored patch can be unsafe, and a generated patch can be excellent; both need evidence appropriate to the affected system.</data>
      <data key="k446">3e6233a86dff27d9d33a4a63b63029e56c6b1ab5286c89bd81623edf2ffe3025</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W069", "W073", "W088"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0102">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0102","kind":"cited_passage","label":"The review-trace denominator is particularly important. Duma et al.~\\autocite{W065} report that 61.38\\% of 33,596 agent-authored PRs have no recorded review, an","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">The review-trace denominator is particularly important. Duma et al.~\autocite{W065} report that 61.38\% of 33,596 agent-authored PRs have no recorded review, an</data>
      <data key="k263">41</data>
      <data key="k265">41</data>
      <data key="k306">The review-trace denominator is particularly important. Duma et al.~\autocite{W065} report that 61.38\% of 33,596 agent-authored PRs have no recorded review, and 84.0\% have no recorded review or only agent review. This is not proof that no human inspected the code: unrecorded discussion, local inspection and repository policy can escape the dataset. The same-repository comparison in the source bibliography also gives a much smaller contrast between agent- and human-authored PRs than a headline 84\% figure might suggest. AIDev-derived studies share underlying PR records, so repeated analysis is not independent replication. The full manuscript and sampling procedure must be checked before quoting adjusted comparisons.</data>
      <data key="k446">e37c0ad92246f43b4b2f7286f606a2cbd7a9b92160e78f61bc9bd87134900f46</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W065"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0103">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0103","kind":"cited_passage","label":"A concrete production deployment and a benchmark answer different questions. Tantithamthavorn et al.~\\autocite{W074} describe an Atlassian RovoDev reviewer depl","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">A concrete production deployment and a benchmark answer different questions. Tantithamthavorn et al.~\autocite{W074} describe an Atlassian RovoDev reviewer depl</data>
      <data key="k263">49</data>
      <data key="k265">49</data>
      <data key="k306">A concrete production deployment and a benchmark answer different questions. Tantithamthavorn et al.~\autocite{W074} describe an Atlassian RovoDev reviewer deployment. Their original abstract reports 38.70\% of AI comments followed by code changes, approximately 30.8\% lower PR cycle time, and 35.6\% fewer human-written comments in their evaluated setting. The figures concern review workflow and follow-up action; they are not a measured reduction in escaped defects, and observational deployment confounders remain relevant. Zeng et al.~\autocite{W076} introduce SWRBench with 1,000 manually verified GitHub PRs and project context; benchmark precision and recall measure correspondence with selected ground-truth review issues, not the causal effect of deployment. The original abstracts support this contrast, while exact table cells and publisher pagination still require inspection.</data>
      <data key="k446">935d4f5e57ba4b20e94d92e3aa9c2821437074194733a3876c4cba89f9962f88</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W074", "W076"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0104">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0104","kind":"cited_passage","label":"AI review tools can identify suspicious patterns, propose missing tests and summarize complex diffs. They can also miss defects or invent problems that are not ","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">AI review tools can identify suspicious patterns, propose missing tests and summarize complex diffs. They can also miss defects or invent problems that are not </data>
      <data key="k263">51</data>
      <data key="k265">51</data>
      <data key="k306">AI review tools can identify suspicious patterns, propose missing tests and summarize complex diffs. They can also miss defects or invent problems that are not present. Evaluations of automated code review (\autocite{W074}, \autocite{W106}) and related research \autocite{W081} investigate different aspects of that performance. A benchmark may count detected defects, while a field deployment may count developer reactions or review latency. These endpoints should not be combined into a single accuracy claim.</data>
      <data key="k446">994a28cdfa4556bc8d8fecad1eb17c6248a9cbf663d47364f7bea8f52150867e</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W074", "W081", "W106"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0105">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0105","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Research on review comment quality and developer response (\\autocite{W064}, \\autocite{W098}, \\autocite{W096}) motivates measuring precision, actionability and r","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Research on review comment quality and developer response (\autocite{W064}, \autocite{W098}, \autocite{W096}) motivates measuring precision, actionability and r</data>
      <data key="k263">65</data>
      <data key="k265">65</data>
      <data key="k306">Research on review comment quality and developer response (\autocite{W064}, \autocite{W098}, \autocite{W096}) motivates measuring precision, actionability and review burden separately. The exact empirical rates remain provisional until the original papers are inspected. For the service, a warning that \textquotesingle the policy code may be unsafe\textquotesingle{} is not actionable. A warning that \textquotesingle the adapter retains the v1 €5,000 ceiling while INT-002 requires €3,000 for new requests\textquotesingle{} names an observable mismatch and supplies a path to reproduce it.</data>
      <data key="k446">ef589a2c4406f39296455aebc41adc06a72d46ee699ec0a6adea6b9638916763</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W064", "W096", "W098"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0106">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0106","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Orosz's publicly visible account describes teams reviewing AI-generated comments and routing changes according to their consequences \\oroszcite{P118}. That crea","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Orosz's publicly visible account describes teams reviewing AI-generated comments and routing changes according to their consequences \oroszcite{P118}. That crea</data>
      <data key="k263">70</data>
      <data key="k265">70</data>
      <data key="k306">Orosz's publicly visible account describes teams reviewing AI-generated comments and routing changes according to their consequences \oroszcite{P118}. That creates a further distinction: a human can validate every reported finding without establishing evidence for every material acceptance obligation. A quiet or filtered reviewer is not a coverage certificate.</data>
      <data key="k446">4c09a1e3db6caf875bac95fb9bf261a413aa5ba5bd2d964bdd1e676e7cf2c1e5</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["P118"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0107">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0107","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Xiang et al.~\\autocite{W102} give a particularly useful verification-cost counterexample. On 116 complete-case LiveCodeBench problems, review by Claude changes ","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Xiang et al.~\autocite{W102} give a particularly useful verification-cost counterexample. On 116 complete-case LiveCodeBench problems, review by Claude changes </data>
      <data key="k263">91</data>
      <data key="k265">91</data>
      <data key="k306">Xiang et al.~\autocite{W102} give a particularly useful verification-cost counterexample. On 116 complete-case LiveCodeBench problems, review by Claude changes Codex passing outputs from 83 to 104 (+21), at \$0.443 versus \$0.190 per task; the opposite reviewer ordering lowers Claude's successes from 106 to 96 while increasing modeled inference cost from \$0.226 to \$0.382 per task. Table~2 provides numerator and denominator for independent \emph{percentage arithmetic}, and Table~4 provides discordances for exact McNemar test rechecks. Neither calculation replays the model calls, proves transfer to repository review, or guarantees a cost-effective production policy. A reviewer remains accountable for independent oracles, acceptance and regression risk. Figure~\ref{fig:ch08-research-1} decomposes those net changes into failures fixed and previously passing answers broken. Read each two-letter label as writer then reviewer: the green and red bars must be considered together. More corrections can coexist with regressions, so a review policy needs both counts rather than a tally of helpful comments.</data>
      <data key="k446">c406a6173946c91483fc24466d0f397111e3d012eeb9014be76e14526fdc63c4</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W102"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0108">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0108","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Other work on model self-review \\autocite{W109} and correlated errors \\autocite{W079} reinforces the need to examine the independence of evidence rather than co","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Other work on model self-review \autocite{W109} and correlated errors \autocite{W079} reinforces the need to examine the independence of evidence rather than co</data>
      <data key="k263">99</data>
      <data key="k265">99</data>
      <data key="k306">Other work on model self-review \autocite{W109} and correlated errors \autocite{W079} reinforces the need to examine the independence of evidence rather than count agreeing opinions. In the approval service, the decisive checker is a deterministic test derived from the authorized contract. A second model may inspect the diff and suggest additional counterexamples, but agreement between two models cannot override the high-risk invariant or the replay requirement. The review design should diversify information sources before it diversifies model names.</data>
      <data key="k446">089ca5d926774265429522cb3962701841d1f04eca47e796f8db275ab98cdff9</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W079", "W109"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0109">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0109","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Studies of human interaction with AI review recommendations (\\autocite{W083}, \\autocite{W088}, \\autocite{W091}) explore this question in different settings. The","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Studies of human interaction with AI review recommendations (\autocite{W083}, \autocite{W088}, \autocite{W091}) explore this question in different settings. The</data>
      <data key="k263">119</data>
      <data key="k265">119</data>
      <data key="k306">Studies of human interaction with AI review recommendations (\autocite{W083}, \autocite{W088}, \autocite{W091}) explore this question in different settings. The current draft does not assign them numerical effects without manuscript-level checks. A reviewer may be influenced by a confident explanation, a green badge or an apparently precise severity score. None of those cues establishes that the finding is correct.</data>
      <data key="k446">cbabc166cf047e53c95e786e32a967023e8911d61519e7b10ee205c898dc5a9c</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W083", "W088", "W091"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0110">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0110","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Research on review allocation \\autocite{W093}, intent-aware code critique \\autocite{W099} and review quality \\autocite{W104} supplies relevant context. The chap","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Research on review allocation \autocite{W093}, intent-aware code critique \autocite{W099} and review quality \autocite{W104} supplies relevant context. The chap</data>
      <data key="k263">133</data>
      <data key="k265">133</data>
      <data key="k306">Research on review allocation \autocite{W093}, intent-aware code critique \autocite{W099} and review quality \autocite{W104} supplies relevant context. The chapter\textquotesingle s proposed decision table routes low-risk, well-tested changes to streamlined review; policy-sensitive or security-relevant changes require specialized reviewers and explicit acceptance evidence. A patch with missing intention authority cannot become low-risk simply because it is small.</data>
      <data key="k446">12d5fa232d8363f786a0145b6518628b8df4647c06195a751860bfd8c293b977</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W093", "W099", "W104"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0111">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0111","kind":"cited_passage","label":"\\noindent\\textbf{When ``read the draft'' meets review capacity.} In 2025 Osmani urged engineers to read AI-generated code as a draft, reasoning that inspection ","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">\noindent\textbf{When ``read the draft'' meets review capacity.} In 2025 Osmani urged engineers to read AI-generated code as a draft, reasoning that inspection </data>
      <data key="k263">147</data>
      <data key="k265">147</data>
      <data key="k306">\noindent\textbf{When ``read the draft'' meets review capacity.} In 2025 Osmani urged engineers to read AI-generated code as a draft, reasoning that inspection preserves understanding and prevents plausible mistakes from entering production \osmanicite{O023}. His September 2026 essay \emph{The Code Nobody Reads} instead explores a future where exhaustive line-by-line human reading cannot scale and lower-risk changes pass through stronger automated checks \osmanicite{O001}. The two positions expose a real design question, not a blanket rule to abolish review: what assurance must be retained when human attention becomes selective?</data>
      <data key="k446">4666e4f7acb48e5dbf99eac7e87b8efa7cff84b0cf75342e8c080aef4ef6960e</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["O001", "O023"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0112">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0112","kind":"cited_passage","label":"Research on review outcomes \\autocite{W107} and maintainer rejection of benchmark-passing patches \\autocite{W111} motivates separating technical plausibility fr","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">Research on review outcomes \autocite{W107} and maintainer rejection of benchmark-passing patches \autocite{W111} motivates separating technical plausibility fr</data>
      <data key="k263">156</data>
      <data key="k265">156</data>
      <data key="k306">Research on review outcomes \autocite{W107} and maintainer rejection of benchmark-passing patches \autocite{W111} motivates separating technical plausibility from integration acceptance. \autocite{W105} provides a contrasting view of review tooling, but its detailed findings remain pending verification. The approval-service dossier includes the INT-001 and INT-002 contracts, the architecture decision, the patch hash, independent test results, the reviewer\textquotesingle s disposition of findings and an explicit acceptance field. Because the laboratory has no real policy-owner signature, its final state remains \textquotesingle ready for review\textquotesingle, not production accepted.</data>
      <data key="k446">bcee231e8399b33764c07f7595ed6e6cfa81912c6dcbeacedbaddafc7f4da354</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["W105", "W107", "W111"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0113">
