      <data key="k248">Corrigendum: 40 Years of Designing Code Comprehension Experiments: A Systematic Mapping Study</data>
      <data key="k281">["C:C10"]</data>
      <data key="k282">Final 13.7.1 active EN/ITA source tree; index links and nocite are not chapter citations</data>
      <data key="k283">true</data>
      <data key="k296">W162Corrigendum2026</data>
      <data key="k453">https://doi.org/10.1145/3838282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0138">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0138","kind":"cited_passage","label":"\\noindent\\textbf{Keep the reasoning repetitions.} Osmani's account of skill decay \\osmanicite{O003} argues that fast autonomous implementation can displace the ","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">\noindent\textbf{Keep the reasoning repetitions.} Osmani's account of skill decay \osmanicite{O003} argues that fast autonomous implementation can displace the </data>
      <data key="k263">122</data>
      <data key="k265">122</data>
      <data key="k306">\noindent\textbf{Keep the reasoning repetitions.} Osmani's account of skill decay \osmanicite{O003} argues that fast autonomous implementation can displace the practice through which developers learn to predict, debug and explain systems. His ``80\% problem'' \osmanicite{O017} describes an evolving work mix; it is not evidence that a developer loses 80\% of competence. Translate the concern into observable learning behavior rather than a second, unvalidated score: before delegating, write a prediction for one boundary case; after execution, inspect a failure or risky diff; explain the relevant invariant without reading the agent's summary; and attempt an unseen related change without assistance at the scheduled Day-14 follow-up.</data>
      <data key="k446">a0432fe192e00964f80382efa553f02e655249f42db8237682530ee2395316d9</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["O003", "O017"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0139">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"","category":"reader","collection":null,"id":"V10:TEXTREF:0139","kind":"cited_passage","label":"There is a competing hypothesis. In Orosz's moderated discussion, Kent Beck argues that assistance can amplify learning \\oroszcite{P123}. This is an experienced","limitation":"","mapped":[],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":""}</data>
      <data key="k150">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
      <data key="k162">CLAIM</data>
      <data key="k246">cited_passage</data>
      <data key="k248">There is a competing hypothesis. In Orosz's moderated discussion, Kent Beck argues that assistance can amplify learning \oroszcite{P123}. This is an experienced</data>
      <data key="k263">128</data>
      <data key="k265">128</data>
      <data key="k306">There is a competing hypothesis. In Orosz's moderated discussion, Kent Beck argues that assistance can amplify learning \oroszcite{P123}. This is an experienced practitioner's expectation, not a measured retention effect. Set it beside Osmani's concern: assistance might sustain prediction, explanation and experimentation, or substitute for those activities. The study should permit improvement, deterioration or no detectable difference rather than presuppose decay.</data>
      <data key="k446">1986682b3932151aeef181f524cd73a3d26172c94878b01c5d85567b133e1bed</data>
      <data key="k463">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k466">["P123"]</data>
      <data key="k487">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V10:TEXTREF:0140">
