      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Birgitta Böckeler","category":null,"collection":"F","id":"F004","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"In-line assistance - how can it get in the way?","limitation":"Qualitative examples and interpretive mechanisms, not measured frequencies of bias or review fatigue.","mapped":["C:C05","C:C08","C:C09"],"printed":false,"streams":["T:Verification &amp; review","T:System knowledge &amp; memory","T:Code quality &amp; security"],"summary":"Describes assistants repeating poor patterns from their context and the burden of continually judging suggestions. Relates these experiences to automation bias, anchoring and reluctance to discard generated work.","topics":["K:Automation bias and trust","K:Human cognitive load","K:Agent context and persistent memory"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/04-coding-assistance-how-in-the-way.html","volumes":[],"year":"2023-08-03"}</data>
