    <node id="F008">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C03"],"authors":"Birgitta Böckeler","category":null,"collection":"F","historical_v12_actual":[],"historical_v12_printed":false,"id":"F008","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"How to tackle unreliability of coding assistants","limitation":"Personal heuristics rather than calibrated reliability estimates; informal numerical intuitions are not treated as measured rates.","mapped":["C:C03","C:C07","C:C08","C:C13"],"printed":true,"streams":["T:Verification &amp; review","T:What agents can do"],"summary":"Frames confidence in assistance around feedback, the developer’s ability to check an answer and the consequences of error. Proposes timeboxing unproductive assistance and retaining responsibility for the result.","topics":["K:Agent failure and escalation","K:Independent verification and oracles","K:Automation bias and trust"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/08-how-to-tackle-unreliability.html","volumes":[],"year":"2023-11-29"}</data>
