      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Matteo Vaccari","category":null,"collection":"F","id":"F020","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"Partner with the AI, throw away the code","limitation":"A single client case; code-acceptance rate is questioned, but a general AI-caused productivity gain is not measured.","mapped":["C:C02","C:C05","C:C10","C:C12"],"printed":false,"streams":["T:Productivity","T:Skills &amp; learning","T:Economics"],"summary":"In a Go/MySQL performance investigation, generated helpers, experiments and unsuccessful rewrites helped the developer understand the problem before rewriting the core solution. Useful assistance can therefore leave little accepted generated code.","topics":["K:Output versus shipped value","K:Evaluation methodology and baselines","K:System understanding and rationale"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/partner-with-ai-and-throw-away-the-code.html","volumes":[],"year":"2025-07-31"}</data>
