      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Birgitta Böckeler","category":null,"collection":"F","id":"F028","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"Viability of local models for coding","limitation":"A personal hardware/tool snapshot. Explanations for observed configuration differences are hypotheses; code quality was not systematically evaluated.","mapped":["C:C03","C:C09","C:C12"],"printed":false,"streams":["T:What agents can do","T:Economics","T:System knowledge &amp; memory"],"summary":"Frames local agentic coding as a combined hardware, model, runtime, context and tool-calling problem. The account separates being able to run a model from obtaining usable results.","topics":["K:Agent context and persistent memory","K:Economic costs and return","K:Evaluation methodology and baselines"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/local-models-for-coding-factors.html","volumes":[],"year":"2026-07-07"}</data>
