      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Birgitta Böckeler","category":null,"collection":"F","id":"F029","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"Experiences with local models for coding","limitation":"Two principal JavaScript/TypeScript tasks and small uneven repeat counts; one-shot automated trials differ from interactive work and do not establish a general ranking.","mapped":["C:C02","C:C03","C:C09","C:C12"],"printed":false,"streams":["T:What agents can do","T:Productivity","T:System knowledge &amp; memory"],"summary":"Presents a viability funnel and compares manual trials, a small automated evaluation and everyday local-model use. Outcome sensitivity to task, context and configuration makes simple capability claims difficult.","topics":["K:Benchmarks and construct validity","K:Evaluation methodology and baselines","K:Agent context and persistent memory"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/local-models-for-coding-experiences.html","volumes":[],"year":"2026-07-08"}</data>
