    <node id="F031">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":[],"authors":"Birgitta Böckeler","category":null,"collection":"F","historical_v12_printed":false,"id":"F031","kind":"practitioner_essay","label":"TDD inside the agent loop - theater or actual value?","limitation":"Small greenfield tasks, imperfect adherence and an LLM-defined quality rubric. Reported aggregate tokens include cache rereads and are not equivalent to billed cost; no universal conclusion about human-led TDD follows.","mapped":["C:C03","C:C07","C:C12","C:C13"],"printed":true,"streams":["T:Verification &amp; review","T:Economics"],"summary":"Separates human-authored tests, a human review checkpoint and TDD entirely inside an agent loop. The small exploratory comparison found no clear advantage for fully internal TDD in model-judged quality or mutation scores.","topics":["K:Independent verification and oracles","K:Evaluation methodology and baselines","K:Economic costs and return"],"url":"https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/tdd-in-the-agent-loop.html","volumes":[],"year":"2026-08-10"}</data>
      <data key="k128">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
      <data key="k129">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
      <data key="k135">IN_PUBLISHED_NDSE2_BIBLIOGRAPHY</data>
      <data key="k162">F</data>
      <data key="k168">Separates human-authored tests, a human review checkpoint and TDD entirely inside an agent loop. The small exploratory comparison found no clear advantage for fully internal TDD in model-judged quality or mutation scores.</data>
      <data key="k184">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
      <data key="k197">["C:C03", "C:C07", "C:C12", "C:C13"]</data>
      <data key="k207">Small exploratory agent evaluation</data>
      <data key="k230">NOT_ADDED_TO_BOOK</data>
      <data key="k246">practitioner_essay</data>
      <data key="k248">TDD inside the agent loop - theater or actual value?</data>
      <data key="k260">Small greenfield tasks, imperfect adherence and an LLM-defined quality rubric. Reported aggregate tokens include cache rereads and are not equivalent to billed cost; no universal conclusion about human-led TDD follows.</data>
      <data key="k273">Independent editorial mapping, not classification by the article authors or SE@PoliMi</data>
