    <node id="NDSE2:C01">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C01"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C01","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"AI Changes the Unit of Software Work","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C01"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Defines an accepted, operable change as the unit of engineering work. The approval-routing case separates business intention, implementation, verification and acceptance, showing why brownfield understanding and explicit decision rights still matter when an AI agent generates the patch.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C01</data>
      <data key="k155">1</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">AI Changes the Unit of Software Work</data>
      <data key="k256">["distinguere un artefatto di implementazione da una modifica accettata", "identificare le persone e le evidenze necessarie tra la richiesta e la release", "delimitare il task affidato a un assistente AI senza delegargli l'autorità sulle decisioni di business"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["distinguish an implementation artifact from an accepted change", "name the people and evidence required between a request and release", "scope an AI assistant's task without delegating business authority"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">277ec2181a885dfee7268a6d504503c8c039a8cc6c8201bfd2a966515d5b2500</data>
      <data key="k478">e89175da618cfae5b422e16c8e01fd457d1da8308a5d9359a2b6aac592cf63ca</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Defines an accepted, operable change as the unit of engineering work. The approval-routing case separates business intention, implementation, verification and acceptance, showing why brownfield understanding and explicit decision rights still matter when an AI agent generates the patch.</data>
      <data key="k494">Definisce il cambiamento accettato e gestibile come unità del lavoro ingegneristico. Il caso di instradamento delle approvazioni distingue intenzione di business, implementazione, verifica e accettazione, mostrando il ruolo della comprensione del sistema e delle responsabilità decisionali anche quando la patch viene generata da un agent.</data>
      <data key="k498">AI Changes the Unit of Software Work</data>
      <data key="k500">L'AI cambia l'unità di lavoro della software engineering</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
