    <node id="NDSE2:C03">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C03"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C03","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"Limits and Capability of Coding Agents","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C03"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Turns agent capability into a bounded engineering hypothesis. Permissions, tools, budgets, stopping rules and escalation constrain execution; the chapter compares execution routes and parallel work while keeping technical completion separate from authorized acceptance.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C03</data>
      <data key="k155">3</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">Limits and Capability of Coding Agents</data>
      <data key="k256">["tradurre una richiesta di lavoro in un envelope di permessi e budget", "distinguere un suggerimento del modello da un'azione autorizzata dall'orchestrator", "fermare un agent o portare un caso in escalation, senza confondere completamento tecnico e accettazione"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["translate a task request into a permission and budget envelope", "tell a model suggestion from an orchestrator-authorized action", "stop or escalate an agent without confusing technical completion with acceptance"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">ce0ca41e0ce359c1fd4752f2db1de6b1312c006510fc9c3ba364e3310916c2b1</data>
      <data key="k478">2c1ae14b69644084668fec3494a975a6f6be7822e77d7d96d1b21f654d2aa713</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Turns agent capability into a bounded engineering hypothesis. Permissions, tools, budgets, stopping rules and escalation constrain execution; the chapter compares execution routes and parallel work while keeping technical completion separate from authorized acceptance.</data>
      <data key="k494">Trasforma la capacità degli agent in un'ipotesi ingegneristica delimitata. Permessi, strumenti, budget, condizioni di arresto ed escalation vincolano l'esecuzione; il capitolo confronta percorsi operativi e lavoro parallelo distinguendo il completamento tecnico dall'accettazione autorizzata.</data>
      <data key="k498">Limits and Capability of Coding Agents</data>
      <data key="k500">Limiti e capacità dei coding agent</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
