      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C05"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C05","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"Quality, Architecture and Maintainability","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C05"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Separates immediate correctness from architectural fit and maintenance obligations. Through duplication, post-merge evidence and a second change to the running service, it develops fitness checks and explicit stewardship instead of treating a passing test suite as complete quality assurance.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C05</data>
      <data key="k155">5</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">Quality, Architecture and Maintainability</data>
      <data key="k256">["sottoporre il codice generato a review non solo per la correttezza immediata, ma anche per la coerenza architetturale", "scrivere controlli di fitness per gli invarianti critici del sistema", "individuare chi si occuperà della manutenzione quando l'agent e il reviewer originari non saranno più disponibili"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["review generated code for architectural fit as well as immediate correctness", "write fitness checks for critical system invariants", "locate who will maintain the result when the original agent and reviewer are gone"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">f6e123ae06931297b82554424c5b9b9c4b6bdb00e897814d515d11203e684075</data>
      <data key="k478">31ceb5547ea22913089d9eba92093a622b30f98f3052e9a0f793dee86df8938e</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Separates immediate correctness from architectural fit and maintenance obligations. Through duplication, post-merge evidence and a second change to the running service, it develops fitness checks and explicit stewardship instead of treating a passing test suite as complete quality assurance.</data>
      <data key="k494">Distingue la correttezza immediata dalla coerenza architetturale e dagli obblighi di manutenzione. Duplicazioni, evidenze successive al merge e un secondo cambiamento al servizio guidano controlli di adeguatezza e responsabilità di manutenzione esplicite.</data>
      <data key="k498">Quality, Architecture and Maintainability</data>
      <data key="k500">Qualità, architettura e manutenibilità</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
