    <node id="NDSE2:C06">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C06"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C06","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"Securing Generated Code and Agent Runtimes","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C06"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Threat-models two distinct surfaces: the generated application and the agent runtime. Dependency provenance, prompt injection, tool permissions and external services become enforceable boundaries, with security evidence tied to the release decision.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C06</data>
      <data key="k155">6</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">Securing Generated Code and Agent Runtimes</data>
      <data key="k256">["costruire threat model distinti per il prodotto generato e per il runtime dell'agent", "far rispettare i permessi dei tool indipendentemente dalle istruzioni incorporate nei file", "specificare le evidenze necessarie prima di accettare una patch sensibile dal punto di vista della sicurezza"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["threat-model the generated product and the agent runtime separately", "enforce tool permissions independently of instructions embedded in files", "specify the evidence required before accepting a security-sensitive patch"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">3af782fd4b06529539e8b78e95b77ad3911980472e272fe111ddcfcc82ce777a</data>
      <data key="k478">f4a3e1c62eae1528ce10817e76376558b41cdc7a6d337397c394cc5cb840ea9e</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Threat-models two distinct surfaces: the generated application and the agent runtime. Dependency provenance, prompt injection, tool permissions and external services become enforceable boundaries, with security evidence tied to the release decision.</data>
      <data key="k494">Analizza due superfici di attacco distinte: l'applicazione generata e il runtime dell'agent. Provenienza delle dipendenze, prompt injection, permessi degli strumenti e servizi esterni diventano vincoli applicabili, collegando le evidenze di sicurezza alla decisione di rilascio.</data>
      <data key="k498">Securing Generated Code and Agent Runtimes</data>
      <data key="k500">Mettere in sicurezza il codice generato e i runtime degli agent</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
