    <node id="NDSE2:C10">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C10"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C10","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"Developer Learning, Mentoring and Comprehension Debt","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C10"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Distinguishes assisted task completion from retained competence. Mentoring, explanations, repairs and deliberate practice lead to delayed retention and transfer checks; proposed competence measures remain instruments to validate rather than established scores.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C10</data>
      <data key="k155">10</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">Developer Learning, Mentoring and Comprehension Debt</data>
      <data key="k256">["distinguere il completamento di un task dall'apprendimento necessario per mantenerlo", "progettare verifiche differite della retention e del transfer", "assegnare responsabilità significative agli sviluppatori junior senza presentare punteggi di competenza non validati come misure consolidate"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["distinguish finishing a task from learning to maintain it", "design delayed retention and transfer checks", "give junior developers meaningful responsibility without treating unvalidated competence scores as established measures"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">8c1523efe9ff14e391995db26334a679c629258003f891389e55b9183e57f36f</data>
      <data key="k478">6222bf93c5aaff838c33613a03d0e0cbf6bd5a8ac293616b215d9ee5fd534e7f</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Distinguishes assisted task completion from retained competence. Mentoring, explanations, repairs and deliberate practice lead to delayed retention and transfer checks; proposed competence measures remain instruments to validate rather than established scores.</data>
      <data key="k494">Distingue il completamento assistito di un compito dalla competenza conservata. Mentoring, spiegazioni, correzioni e pratica deliberata conducono a verifiche differite di ritenzione e trasferimento; le misure di competenza proposte restano strumenti da validare.</data>
      <data key="k498">Developer Learning, Mentoring and Comprehension Debt</data>
      <data key="k500">Apprendimento, mentoring e debito di comprensione degli sviluppatori</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
