    <node id="NDSE2:C12">
      <data key="k121">{"actual":["C:C12"],"authors":"Enrico Papalini","category":null,"collection":"N","id":"NDSE2:C12","kind":"published_book_chapter","label":"Economics, Jobs, Risk and Evidence-Based Adoption","limitation":"Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.","mapped":["C:C12"],"printed":false,"streams":[],"summary":"Evaluates the economics of the whole engineering loop, including human effort, failed attempts, maintenance and risk. Employment evidence and alternative explanations remain separate from forecasts; adoption requires a counterfactual, uncertainty bounds and a reversal condition.","topics":[],"url":"","volumes":["V06"],"year":"2026"}</data>
      <data key="k126">Enrico Papalini</data>
      <data key="k153">C:C12</data>
      <data key="k155">12</data>
      <data key="k192">EDITION:NDSE2:13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k207">Published author chapter; engineering synthesis</data>
      <data key="k246">published_book_chapter</data>
      <data key="k248">Economics, Jobs, Risk and Evidence-Based Adoption</data>
      <data key="k256">["calcolare il costo dell'intero loop, e non soltanto quello dei token", "distinguere le osservazioni sull'occupazione dalle previsioni causali", "formulare una decisione di adozione dell'AI con controfattuale, incertezza e condizione di rollback espliciti"]</data>
      <data key="k257">["calculate full-loop rather than token-only cost", "separate employment observations from causal forecasts", "frame an AI adoption decision with an explicit counterfactual, uncertainty and rollback condition"]</data>
      <data key="k260">Author engineering synthesis and teaching material; publication is not independent empirical validation.</data>
      <data key="k285">NDSE2_PUBLISHED_EDITION_20261018</data>
      <data key="k390">Author-supplied final EN/ITA 13.7.1 LaTeX sources; publication confirmed by the author on 2026-10-18.</data>
      <data key="k398">PUBLISHED_AUTHOR_CONFIRMED</data>
      <data key="k463">EN/chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k464">ITA/chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k477">86c0ede476fd2a1b32d32f4ea86297429dd24aad34db3f6c7540431e1190ccbe</data>
      <data key="k478">d1598543866ce040908920e04662bc2ffa6ff1831a4cf984240911bf9cd54924</data>
      <data key="k481">13.7.1</data>
      <data key="k493">Evaluates the economics of the whole engineering loop, including human effort, failed attempts, maintenance and risk. Employment evidence and alternative explanations remain separate from forecasts; adoption requires a counterfactual, uncertainty bounds and a reversal condition.</data>
      <data key="k494">Valuta l'economia dell'intero ciclo ingegneristico, includendo lavoro umano, tentativi falliti, manutenzione e rischio. Mantiene separate evidenze sul lavoro, spiegazioni alternative e previsioni; l'adozione richiede un controfattuale, limiti d'incertezza e una condizione di reversibilità.</data>
      <data key="k498">Economics, Jobs, Risk and Evidence-Based Adoption</data>
      <data key="k500">Economia, lavoro, rischio e adozione basata sulle evidenze</data>
      <data key="k513">V06</data>
    </node>
