    </edge>
    <edge id="x06029" source="EDITION:WOP:JPG:V7:20261011" target="JPG:V7:29">
      <data key="k523">x06029</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v7_rendition"</data>
      <data key="k596">JPG_EDITION_V7</data>
      <data key="k603">HAS_JPG_RENDITION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06030" source="EDITION:WOP:JPG:V7:20261011" target="JPG:V7:30">
      <data key="k523">x06030</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v7_rendition"</data>
      <data key="k596">JPG_EDITION_V7</data>
      <data key="k603">HAS_JPG_RENDITION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06031" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="EDITION:WOP:JPG:V7:20261011">
      <data key="k523">x06031</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_editorial_revision"</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k603">EDITORIAL_REVISION_OF</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06032" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:01">
      <data key="k523">x06032</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">9cfa250f556c24921cdf72c40ba4ccce43704e66851be7928a04396edebd45a8</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">79d183c9ce2ab7cbf5cf7e0f9a288adce4ec6a5fb04fe69d548e29d29f8bc739</data>
      <data key="k600">The timeline in Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-research-1} can be read as an expansion of engineering concerns, rather than a succession of methods that erase their predecessors. Agentic work still needs the process, risk and operational disciplines represented to its left. The emerging engineer's role therefore includes decomposing a problem, choosing what may safely be delegated, building independent checks and making the reasoning behind acceptance available to other people. Which activities grow or shrink under AI adoption remains a research question; the conceptual distinction is between authorship of an artifact and responsibility for its consequences.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01-the-engineers-work-before-and-after-ai</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06033" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:02">
      <data key="k523">x06033</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">f5f8cdfafee11b9aba93846e769f36b97fbba48218a8f6ad21bf3319711bd1fe</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">79d183c9ce2ab7cbf5cf7e0f9a288adce4ec6a5fb04fe69d548e29d29f8bc739</data>
      <data key="k600">The return path in Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-research-2} makes the lifecycle revisable: operational experience can reopen requirements, while human control spans every stage rather than appearing only at the end. An approved intention is a living, versioned contract for a bounded change. If a policy owner clarifies an approval threshold after implementation, the new fact enters as an authorized delta. The team then revisits the affected design assumptions, tests and knowledge records, retaining earlier evidence for the earlier version. This selective invalidation keeps the workflow incremental rather than restarting the entire lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01-the-lifecycle-of-a-trustworthy-change</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06034" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:03">
      <data key="k523">x06034</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-change-acceptance</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">692331aa186da6e22ab998fc1cc411ec1cce93bcddc6f263b2bee42fc3f0f35c</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d18766d3a039137e8bc0ef533f694feb6550f919764dd52e477858f04ed87402</data>
      <data key="k600">Return to the request to make a department's approval ceiling configurable. An agent can produce a patch before anyone has decided whether ``approval'' means eligibility, escalation or final authorization. To prevent that ambiguity from becoming a hidden software rule, trace the request through a sequence of decisions, each with a different source of authority. In Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-change-acceptance}, the patch sits between authorization and verification; the role labels beneath the boxes identify who is responsible for each decision. Moving right requires the corresponding evidence or approval, not merely another artifact from the maker.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06035" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:04">
      <data key="k523">x06035</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch02-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">5e12e33917104b3e58a65a1d58a31f5d8f055e3862d1017b55695fdbcc29aa8e</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter02.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">aa2d769d45a928d9abea63a9b54f7c7ad0cc701af5c2d67cb9fc331fa1827d74</data>
      <data key="k600">Two experiments can disagree without one being defective. Becker and colleagues studied sixteen experienced open-source developers completing 246 tasks in repositories they knew well. In their early-2025 tool setting, allowing AI increased completion time by about 19\%. Developers had expected acceleration, and after participating still believed the tool had helped. Paradis and colleagues\textquotesingle{} Google trial instead estimated a roughly 21\% reduction in task time in its own environment. \autocite{W023,W008} Figure~\ref{fig:ch02-research-1} isolates the first study's disagreement: both subjective estimates fall below zero, meaning less task time, while the measured effect is above zero. Retrospective confidence therefore remains a different signal from timed performance.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch02-why-controlled-studies-disagree</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06036" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:05">
      <data key="k523">x06036</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch02-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">15d718b28cd04e101fafd658a6fa5b135b2edcaf3dcacf56d9ea8be94c57129e</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter02.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">aa2d769d45a928d9abea63a9b54f7c7ad0cc701af5c2d67cb9fc331fa1827d74</data>
      <data key="k600">The redistribution in Figure~\ref{fig:ch02-research-2} explains why the service pilot must record supervision as well as construction: prompting, waiting and reviewing outputs become part of the task. The rectangles name activities, not equal amounts of time or measured savings. Collect short post-task reports on perceived effort, confidence and comprehension alongside independently logged time, including test repairs and stakeholder clarification. An engineer who finishes faster but loses understanding of the policy may create future costs. Chapter~\ref{chap:10} returns to that learning question; the pilot should preserve the signal rather than discard it.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch02-developer-experience-and-hidden-time</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06037" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:06">
      <data key="k523">x06037</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch03-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">6fe08ee1cf9b7d33718d10a3003f11d2cf2e898cb509c87edaff3e97ec6ed3be</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The exchange in Figure~\ref{fig:ch03-research-1} connects human intent and acceptance with the agent's bounded execution through versioned evidence packs. For the service, the outgoing task carries the contract and permissions; the returning pack contains the candidate diff and a trace of what was read and executed. The feedback paths let either side request clarification without turning a tool result into policy. This separation lets us evaluate capability without granting merge, release or policy-approval authority.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-from-suggestion-to-a-permission-bounded-agent</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06038" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:07">
      <data key="k523">x06038</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:osmani-agency-orchestration</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">4c23ec34588bc09586f6d8281501be33899a2bcca1e8ec29f7df02e5b3b64a73</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The position on Figure~\ref{fig:osmani-agency-orchestration} never supplies its own approval. For each configuration, record the writable scope, expected independent evidence, rollback mechanism, review capacity and named acceptance owner. Expand either axis only when observed accepted outcomes justify the added complexity; a higher level is not automatically better.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-the-task-envelope</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06039" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:08">
      <data key="k523">x06039</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch03-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">ad64302d8ef6bfaebc686143bcdff6dba51ff91a6e3c09be7306f032d426540b</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The spread in Figure~\ref{fig:ch03-research-2} illustrates why task mix matters: documentation changes had a higher merged share than performance changes in the sampled corpus. The bars summarize repository and reviewer decisions, not probabilities for our next task. They motivate separate evaluation of task classes, while leaving the causes of the differences open.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-agent-benchmarks-and-observed-pull-requests</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06040" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:09">
      <data key="k523">x06040</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:controls_execution_P110</data>
      <data key="k563">3</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">2</data>
      <data key="k592">a973d015dc2104ca0411b7e528272c5ef1d02d280fdd73ea6f8248a5faeeceb3</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">For the same INT-002 task, first name the control missing from the simpler route. Is it a permission check, durable progress state, independent evidence, or an escalation path? Add a mechanism only with a testable account of how it supplies that control. Where the simpler route already meets the contract, extra scheduling or coordination is an additional maintenance obligation rather than a maturity achievement. Figure~\ref{fig:controls_execution_P110} separates these decisions.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-a-bounded-proposeactobserve-loop</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06041" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:10">
      <data key="k523">x06041</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">ec1604bafd55a8fc85775bf158c8683e65352c3ea14fb5c6c95f8b6f3b0f4309</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">5280faf997ec1bb32a7160d02c323a9a203a75e0cfccceb64cd8b481810b7aa4</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-research-1} shows where the ledger enters execution. The authorized contract constrains deterministic workflow code; the model contributes subtask content and uses only the permitted tools. The right-hand ``verified result'' denotes an output checked within that scope, not authorization to change the contract or release the service. Behavioral examples must supply the expectations against which such an output is judged.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04-from-a-request-to-a-versioned-intention-ledger</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06042" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:11">
      <data key="k523">x06042</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">31d5a95b7efee7b1f7427ad193ba84c1073f94aaab7d7af9d27f50367edf6f59</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">5280faf997ec1bb32a7160d02c323a9a203a75e0cfccceb64cd8b481810b7aa4</data>
      <data key="k600">Hassan\textquotesingle s roadmap \autocite{W152} and research on rejected agent PRs \autocite{W071} motivate coordination and review without establishing an optimal gate sequence. Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-research-2} makes our proposed sequence explicit: validate the authorized delta before asking the model for a new patch, then rerun the affected contracts and independent checks. The dashed return brings unresolved evidence back to the control layer; it does not let the model silently rewrite intention. This keeps a late requirement small enough to trace without regenerating the entire system.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04-a-delta-driven-iterative-brownfield-lifecycle</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06043" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:12">
      <data key="k523">x06043</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-invalidation-loop</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">a80039c8696e1dd4b0b4a79179f3e141495a22d9984583888a21bf6b7f128412</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d2c109d282dc74603d2072cf2de3ffd75db3b2859a785600f00ee7ad98eb421e</data>
      <data key="k600">The return arrow in Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-invalidation-loop} starts another impact analysis after the next delta is authorized; it does not reopen every invariant. For the change in the table, invalidate the Treasury boundary fixture and its new-decision tests, while retaining replay, audit, cross-border and high-risk obligations. The checker derives expected behavior from INT-002, not from the maker's patch. Exercise~\ref{ex:ch04} asks you to author this change ledger. Research-versus-proposal distinctions are in Appendix~\ref{app:methodology}, \S\ref{app:commentary-ch04}.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06044" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:13">
      <data key="k523">x06044</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch05-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">7706b54a97c030fd16787f3953e3463af9f3bfa831eae52f48c243e2b5885f1a</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">76344b570df88cc78f651c5b435916b41ff1ecfb56d0133e1f08bb5b028e801e</data>
      <data key="k600">Before adopting a headline number, inspect the numerator and denominator: warnings per function or per thousand lines, code samples or accepted patches, total findings or high-severity findings, generated candidates or deployed changes. A matched sample can still be biased if a docstring omits the surrounding repository\textquotesingle s constraints. Conversely, an observational comparison of merged pull requests may exclude failed proposals and hide review effort. The engineering lesson is to match the study design to the question, then preserve its limitations in the citation. Read Figure~\ref{fig:ch05-research-1} in that order: corpus selection, enrichment, measurement and validation determine what a quality claim can mean. Its final box concerns statistical and sensitivity checks on the analysis, not certification that the merged software is safe in production.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch05-reading-ai-versus-human-studies-correctly</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06045" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:14">
      <data key="k523">x06045</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch05-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">13e3bf068c852a38af6e80d17d55ee06ae76b27e1319b76c13020b9ccfbffacc</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">76344b570df88cc78f651c5b435916b41ff1ecfb56d0133e1f08bb5b028e801e</data>
      <data key="k600">A separate comparison, summarized in Figure~\ref{fig:ch05-research-2}, groups repositories by prior AI-tool exposure. Its velocity row differs between the agent-first and IDE-first cohorts, while both show worsened maintainability signals in the summarized estimates. The aligned boxes compare directions, not equal effect sizes. For our service, the lesson is to track later change effort alongside immediate output rather than let a velocity gain stand in for maintainability.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch05-post-merge-evolution-and-maintenance-burden</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06046" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:15">
      <data key="k523">x06046</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch06-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">be01d6c2ea166e8f5c23365438e8be5bdc883d213a7690527adb5faf8e2a6ffc</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c0e22a9113e0fd8bfc4f632c25df153a2756fcb3bf726534a5713a93ece6fa2</data>
      <data key="k600">The critical transition in Figure~\ref{fig:ch06-research-1} is from a suggested name to an installed artifact: a name becoming available in a registry does not establish its trustworthiness. The control beneath the path therefore combines existence checks with provenance and locked dependencies. Our proposed gate requires approved identity and version review before installation, including for tool servers and skills. Pinning limits ambiguity but does not establish integrity. The teaching laboratory checks only a local manifest; it does not resolve or install packages over the network.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch06-dependency-provenance-and-hallucinated-packages</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06047" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:16">
      <data key="k523">x06047</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch06-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">3f78cc4849524089d8ee791fbf9b6bbdb2ce323d02e5648f14fe7cb659341edd</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c0e22a9113e0fd8bfc4f632c25df153a2756fcb3bf726534a5713a93ece6fa2</data>
      <data key="k600">Our proposed profile uses explicit tool operations, no wildcard shell grants, no default network egress, pinned tool declarations and structured audit logs. Skills and servers are reviewed like other executable dependencies; a friendly description is not an authorization. The laboratory rejects a manifest containing a floating tool version or broad shell permission and accepts a narrowly scoped manifest. It does not execute or authenticate any remote MCP server. The fork in Figure~\ref{fig:ch06-research-2} places enforcement after interpretation: even when the model accepts an instruction from a repository file, the runtime must separately allow the operation or deny its side effect. Reading content and acquiring authority remain distinct events.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch06-harness-configuration-skills-and-external-services</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06048" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:17">
      <data key="k523">x06048</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">12b8c6b6ca538821919bfd1c9f3a6b882e99403d83476af691041b0fd3d5897f</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">1bbb5af2473938ef0cee310a060ecc9a00673ed6daaff11af94ce508d4defcee</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-research-1} makes the conditioning in \autocite{W079} important: the bars compare how often two models choose the same wrong answer \emph{given that both are wrong}. They do not show how often the models fail overall. Agreement above the uniform wrong-choice baseline warns against treating consensus as independent evidence. Together with evaluator self-preference in broader LLM judgments \autocite{W082}, it motivates diversifying evidence sources; its quantitative transfer to software defect detection remains unverified.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07-independent-checkers-and-correlated-error</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06049" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:18">
      <data key="k523">x06049</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">640454a5b25b369e6987867b3193dc4615ca7c931fc1aef66bd43af80253cdab</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">1bbb5af2473938ef0cee310a060ecc9a00673ed6daaff11af94ce508d4defcee</data>
      <data key="k600">Every attempt retains a task identifier, code hash, tool version, diff, tests, failure reason, time or cost budget and resulting state. \autocite{W101}, \autocite{W095} and \autocite{W151} motivate caution about self-review and policy separation, but do not validate this exact retry policy. The steps in Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-research-2} represent distinct obligations: establish scope and contract, test behavior, review the evidence, and decide on release. Passing the test-oracle step does not satisfy the neighboring obligations. The staircase is a checklist of evidence boundaries, not a calibrated rise in reliability.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07-bounded-repair-versus-independent-acceptance</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06050" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:19">
      <data key="k523">x06050</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-independent-oracle</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">39133958ed6af4dc0bcbad476377880b1273fad5290d9063e78efb1b2ed17284</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">9e9e6ba0730240be5f7e150066b86a6efb15bd5375f7e17daf7b38c818cc6d00</data>
      <data key="k600">Suppose a maker changes the Treasury ceiling to EUR~3,000 and writes a test that computes its expected result using the very same function under test. The test can pass even if the function ignores the ceiling entirely. The checker must instead receive expected outcomes from an independently approved contract and an external test harness. The two branches in Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-independent-oracle} start from the same authorized contract, rather than deriving the expected answer from the candidate. They converge at the reviewer so that implementation and independently specified expectations can be compared. A second actor alone would not provide that independence.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06051" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:20">
      <data key="k523">x06051</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch08-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">c406a6173946c91483fc24466d0f397111e3d012eeb9014be76e14526fdc63c4</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d3c4f31ca0fde0db8524e4a533adf2001c1488aadddf564cc5b3c37c8c585666</data>
      <data key="k600">Xiang et al.~\autocite{W102} give a particularly useful verification-cost counterexample. On 116 complete-case LiveCodeBench problems, review by Claude changes Codex passing outputs from 83 to 104 (+21), at \$0.443 versus \$0.190 per task; the opposite reviewer ordering lowers Claude's successes from 106 to 96 while increasing modeled inference cost from \$0.226 to \$0.382 per task. Table~2 provides numerator and denominator for independent \emph{percentage arithmetic}, and Table~4 provides discordances for exact McNemar test rechecks. Neither calculation replays the model calls, proves transfer to repository review, or guarantees a cost-effective production policy. A reviewer remains accountable for independent oracles, acceptance and regression risk. Figure~\ref{fig:ch08-research-1} decomposes those net changes into failures fixed and previously passing answers broken. Read each two-letter label as writer then reviewer: the green and red bars must be considered together. More corrections can coexist with regressions, so a review policy needs both counts rather than a tally of helpful comments.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch08-self-review-cross-model-review-and-shared-blind-spots</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06052" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:21">
      <data key="k523">x06052</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch08-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">4f5c742427d0f633b73efc1a0859a1a2450db48d0aef3e221190c6cadab82c2d</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d3c4f31ca0fde0db8524e4a533adf2001c1488aadddf564cc5b3c37c8c585666</data>
      <data key="k600">Cost adds another dimension in Figure~\ref{fig:ch08-research-2}. Each arrow begins at a writer-only baseline; moving right means greater inference cost, while moving up or down means a higher or lower pass rate. The almost horizontal A-to-AA route buys little net change in this sample, and the downward A-to-AO route spends more while losing passes. These are task-level comparisons, not a production cost model, but they expose why an additional review step must earn its place.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch08-self-review-cross-model-review-and-shared-blind-spots</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06053" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:22">
      <data key="k523">x06053</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch09-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">70438904f7aa46d1ba1bd684d2d8b157c9304619340e22fadb749359c7fa3288</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d0d7b46ec9ac8c80f5d51df8f0b25b83bf89ced3daa1eb6c8de701ecbf7dc610</data>
      <data key="k600">The package must record omissions. Finding one threshold constant does not prove there are no other consumers. An old passing test does not prove the current branch passes. A model-generated meeting summary is not an approved contract. Missing facts that affect acceptance should produce questions for the relevant owner, not confident guesses. The branching in Figure~\ref{fig:ch09-research-1} separates a recorded event from the semantic claim drawn from it before retrieval joins them again. Its ``what is true'' label must be read as a version-scoped assertion: observing a v1 decision does not establish the rule for a new v2 request.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch09-context-assembly-for-an-agent</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06054" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:23">
      <data key="k523">x06054</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch09-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">be0a5b5d392e447bf979c79064fc5ddc2de175ef2c0cdf814041fd4a24b543a2</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d0d7b46ec9ac8c80f5d51df8f0b25b83bf89ced3daa1eb6c8de701ecbf7dc610</data>
      <data key="k600">INT-002 invalidates Treasury boundary expectations for new decisions and the current policy-fixture reference. It does not invalidate the high-risk invariant, the OPS threshold or historical idempotency decisions. A graph dependency walk can identify candidate impacts, but a human reviewer must challenge missing edges. The memory system should preserve historical evidence and explicitly identify which checks need rerunning. Figure~\ref{fig:ch09-research-2} addresses a different failure: losing required state during compaction or reset. Typed records pass through a validated writeback journal before durable storage; the lower box requires stopping when that preservation cannot be guaranteed. Preserving a record intact still does not make its contents current or authorized.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch09-memory-consistency-decay-and-invalidation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06055" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:24">
      <data key="k523">x06055</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch10-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">a84a799c02c8ac283917097c4d2b7d2f59d9d52487414e087b89e132871555a4</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">c9de72e9b9cbeeb7a7ab5044994f1de717789bd9e443b6e0e694e6b108ba81e4</data>
      <data key="k600">Following the expert-to-tour-to-learner path in Figure~\ref{fig:ch10-research-1}, a maintainer can curate three stops through the service. First inspect INT-001 and INT-002 and predict the EUR~4,000 Treasury outcome under each revision. Then trace \texttt{ApprovalService.evaluate} and explain why replay does not use the current ceiling. Finally inspect the defective legacy route and identify a contract-derived counterexample to its HIGH-risk behavior. The lower strip turns the tour into a proposed check of independent reasoning: explain an invariant, predict a failure and make an unaided change. Completing the tour is preparation for that check, not proof of durable learning.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch10-learning-through-explanations-repairs-and-code-tours</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06056" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:25">
      <data key="k523">x06056</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch10-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">2</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">66cd0db2d86908b07a1673f1eeebbd583728e249fc7e7fa50f5300dc02ce2cc4</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">c9de72e9b9cbeeb7a7ab5044994f1de717789bd9e443b6e0e694e6b108ba81e4</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch10-research-2} helps separate those outcomes. Its arrow leads from assisted work to an \emph{immediate} unaided quiz, not to a delayed retention measurement. The lower strip describes observed patterns of engagement, not randomly assigned teaching strategies. A mentoring programme can therefore use these observations to frame questions, but needs its own later transfer assessment before claiming that assisted practice produced lasting competence.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch10-mentoring-and-apprenticeship-in-a-team-with-agents</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06057" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:26">
      <data key="k523">x06057</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch11-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">1223702a42063d438c983d72a1d0be637250d5713ebdfd7508f43ed2a8db032f</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter11.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c3012ea9fe30a0ad57c8abb5c046a010f02ea71f46042e2cdf2c6aee47fac90</data>
      <data key="k600">Read the dot matrix in Figure~\ref{fig:ch11-research-1} across each row: filled dots mark provisions appearing together, and the right-hand count belongs to that selected combination. The rows illustrate how rules on contributions can coexist with requirements for human involvement, disclosure and accountability. They are neither a complete sample total nor a recommended policy ranking. For the service, define each obligation explicitly and evaluate the resulting review burden, acceptance quality and unwanted workarounds.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch11-policies-that-make-expectations-visible</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06058" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:27">
      <data key="k523">x06058</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch11-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">befbbaef788ed066d7a0cce32742aec03d7e30fb4bc6257725052a4362129840</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter11.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c3012ea9fe30a0ad57c8abb5c046a010f02ea71f46042e2cdf2c6aee47fac90</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch11-research-2} shows why those controls need a channel-specific scope. The upper bar classifies policies on code contributions; the lower bars record an absence of explicit guidance for communication and issues or security. Silence in a policy is not permission for an agent to post externally or disclose sensitive information. Our gate profile must state these boundaries separately rather than inherit them from a general allowance to submit code.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch11-executable-policy-as-an-engineering-proposal</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06059" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:28">
      <data key="k523">x06059</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch12-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">5f8c0818a87b7b35e479181b8e9bfed0cba3f9653cb849fd6d099013a4b6bf58</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">dbf4854f748601e0dd7778f39625870b36752dac82df792108a48d1b62cc701f</data>
      <data key="k600">The queue in Chapter~\ref{chap:11} gives a local reading of Figure~\ref{fig:ch12-research-1}. Candidate generation feeds review and integration, while the dashed capacity boundary reminds us that downstream delivery can remain constrained. More upstream work then accumulates instead of becoming proportionally more releases. The economic question is whether the intervention expands capacity at the constrained stage or reduces the evidence-gathering effort required there; faster generation alone answers neither.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch12-why-cheap-generation-may-increase-total-cost</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06060" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:29">
      <data key="k523">x06060</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch12-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">60460ac8a1e8eaeb5280e3b165572753501420b4b7b316aeac236285510d09de</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">dbf4854f748601e0dd7778f39625870b36752dac82df792108a48d1b62cc701f</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch12-research-2} places the long-term question on a skill axis. The two curves represent stylized cohorts, and the vertical line marks the model's active-expert threshold $a_t$; neither their relative heights nor their displacement estimates our team's future headcount or competence. The diagram asks how access to expertise changes what a later cohort can learn. Training time, attrition, supervision and delayed competence therefore belong in the investment discussion, but require longitudinal observations rather than numbers read from these illustrative curves.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">ch12-the-apprenticeship-and-long-term-skill-economy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06061" source="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011" target="JPG:V7:30">
      <data key="k523">x06061</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v8_prose_explanation"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:app-evidence-to-teaching</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Editorial linkage, not a new empirical-evidence relation</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">fcf3ab4c21023c5a2c606be7f35657b6d38b320f767456df1ebd2e0e3d79cb9a</data>
      <data key="k596">FIGURE_TEXT_AUDIT_V8</data>
      <data key="k598">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">235189b1ccedc2846cb38b438cb6b31c8878468edf89a52deba6922ba4943c27</data>
      <data key="k600">Follow Figure~\ref{fig:app-evidence-to-teaching} from a publication and its version to a bounded claim before entering the chapter's engineering interpretation. The branch into this appendix retains the claim's qualifications; the dashed link carries limitations into the worked example instead of leaving them behind. Thus a source may motivate a proposed gate without validating it. The graph records that chain of use, not a shortcut from citation to proof.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V8</data>
      <data key="k610">app:graph-construction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06062" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="EDITION:WOP:FIGURE_TEXT:V8:20261011">
      <data key="k523">x06062</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reader_revision"</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k603">READER_REVISION_OF</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06063" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="READER:V9:INTRODUCTION">
      <data key="k523">x06063</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_document"</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k603">HAS_READER_DOCUMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06064" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="READER:V9:SOLUTIONS">
      <data key="k523">x06064</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_document"</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k603">HAS_READER_DOCUMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06065" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="READER:V9:EVIDENCE">
      <data key="k523">x06065</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_document"</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k603">HAS_READER_DOCUMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06066" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:01">
      <data key="k523">x06066</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">9cfa250f556c24921cdf72c40ba4ccce43704e66851be7928a04396edebd45a8</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">79d183c9ce2ab7cbf5cf7e0f9a288adce4ec6a5fb04fe69d548e29d29f8bc739</data>
      <data key="k600">The timeline in Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-research-1} can be read as an expansion of engineering concerns, rather than a succession of methods that erase their predecessors. Agentic work still needs the process, risk and operational disciplines represented to its left. The emerging engineer's role therefore includes decomposing a problem, choosing what may safely be delegated, building independent checks and making the reasoning behind acceptance available to other people. Which activities grow or shrink under AI adoption remains a research question; the conceptual distinction is between authorship of an artifact and responsibility for its consequences.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01-the-engineers-work-before-and-after-ai</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06067" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:02">
      <data key="k523">x06067</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">f5f8cdfafee11b9aba93846e769f36b97fbba48218a8f6ad21bf3319711bd1fe</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">79d183c9ce2ab7cbf5cf7e0f9a288adce4ec6a5fb04fe69d548e29d29f8bc739</data>
      <data key="k600">The return path in Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-research-2} makes the lifecycle revisable: operational experience can reopen requirements, while human control spans every stage rather than appearing only at the end. An approved intention is a living, versioned contract for a bounded change. If a policy owner clarifies an approval threshold after implementation, the new fact enters as an authorized delta. The team then revisits the affected design assumptions, tests and knowledge records, retaining earlier evidence for the earlier version. This selective invalidation keeps the workflow incremental rather than restarting the entire lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01-the-lifecycle-of-a-trustworthy-change</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06068" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:03">
      <data key="k523">x06068</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch01-change-acceptance</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">692331aa186da6e22ab998fc1cc411ec1cce93bcddc6f263b2bee42fc3f0f35c</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked01.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d18766d3a039137e8bc0ef533f694feb6550f919764dd52e477858f04ed87402</data>
      <data key="k600">Return to the request to make a department's approval ceiling configurable. An agent can produce a patch before anyone has decided whether ``approval'' means eligibility, escalation or final authorization. To prevent that ambiguity from becoming a hidden software rule, trace the request through a sequence of decisions, each with a different source of authority. In Figure~\ref{fig:ch01-change-acceptance}, the patch sits between authorization and verification; the role labels beneath the boxes identify who is responsible for each decision. Moving right requires the corresponding evidence or approval, not merely another artifact from the maker.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch01:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06069" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:04">
      <data key="k523">x06069</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch02-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">5e12e33917104b3e58a65a1d58a31f5d8f055e3862d1017b55695fdbcc29aa8e</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter02.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">aa2d769d45a928d9abea63a9b54f7c7ad0cc701af5c2d67cb9fc331fa1827d74</data>
      <data key="k600">Two experiments can disagree without one being defective. Becker and colleagues studied sixteen experienced open-source developers completing 246 tasks in repositories they knew well. In their early-2025 tool setting, allowing AI increased completion time by about 19\%. Developers had expected acceleration, and after participating still believed the tool had helped. Paradis and colleagues\textquotesingle{} Google trial instead estimated a roughly 21\% reduction in task time in its own environment. \autocite{W023,W008} Figure~\ref{fig:ch02-research-1} isolates the first study's disagreement: both subjective estimates fall below zero, meaning less task time, while the measured effect is above zero. Retrospective confidence therefore remains a different signal from timed performance.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch02-why-controlled-studies-disagree</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06070" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:05">
      <data key="k523">x06070</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch02-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">15d718b28cd04e101fafd658a6fa5b135b2edcaf3dcacf56d9ea8be94c57129e</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter02.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">aa2d769d45a928d9abea63a9b54f7c7ad0cc701af5c2d67cb9fc331fa1827d74</data>
      <data key="k600">The redistribution in Figure~\ref{fig:ch02-research-2} explains why the service pilot must record supervision as well as construction: prompting, waiting and reviewing outputs become part of the task. The rectangles name activities, not equal amounts of time or measured savings. Collect short post-task reports on perceived effort, confidence and comprehension alongside independently logged time, including test repairs and stakeholder clarification. An engineer who finishes faster but loses understanding of the policy may create future costs. Chapter~\ref{chap:10} returns to that learning question; the pilot should preserve the signal rather than discard it.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch02-developer-experience-and-hidden-time</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06071" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:06">
      <data key="k523">x06071</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch03-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">6fe08ee1cf9b7d33718d10a3003f11d2cf2e898cb509c87edaff3e97ec6ed3be</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The exchange in Figure~\ref{fig:ch03-research-1} connects human intent and acceptance with the agent's bounded execution through versioned evidence packs. For the service, the outgoing task carries the contract and permissions; the returning pack contains the candidate diff and a trace of what was read and executed. The feedback paths let either side request clarification without turning a tool result into policy. This separation lets us evaluate capability without granting merge, release or policy-approval authority.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-from-suggestion-to-a-permission-bounded-agent</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06072" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:07">
      <data key="k523">x06072</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:osmani-agency-orchestration</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">4c23ec34588bc09586f6d8281501be33899a2bcca1e8ec29f7df02e5b3b64a73</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The position on Figure~\ref{fig:osmani-agency-orchestration} never supplies its own approval. For each configuration, record the writable scope, expected independent evidence, rollback mechanism, review capacity and named acceptance owner. Expand either axis only when observed accepted outcomes justify the added complexity; a higher level is not automatically better.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-the-task-envelope</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06073" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:08">
      <data key="k523">x06073</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch03-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">ad64302d8ef6bfaebc686143bcdff6dba51ff91a6e3c09be7306f032d426540b</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">The spread in Figure~\ref{fig:ch03-research-2} illustrates why task mix matters: documentation changes had a higher merged share than performance changes in the sampled corpus. The bars summarize repository and reviewer decisions, not probabilities for our next task. They motivate separate evaluation of task classes, while leaving the causes of the differences open.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-agent-benchmarks-and-observed-pull-requests</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06074" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:09">
      <data key="k523">x06074</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:controls_execution_P110</data>
      <data key="k563">3</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">2</data>
      <data key="k592">a973d015dc2104ca0411b7e528272c5ef1d02d280fdd73ea6f8248a5faeeceb3</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter03.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">869ad0357050f6dcde42f1990c99209518e90f6574fd264ad71e4da80aa80bbb</data>
      <data key="k600">For the same INT-002 task, first name the control missing from the simpler route. Is it a permission check, durable progress state, independent evidence, or an escalation path? Add a mechanism only with a testable account of how it supplies that control. Where the simpler route already meets the contract, extra scheduling or coordination is an additional maintenance obligation rather than a maturity achievement. Figure~\ref{fig:controls_execution_P110} separates these decisions.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch03-a-bounded-proposeactobserve-loop</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06075" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:10">
      <data key="k523">x06075</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">ec1604bafd55a8fc85775bf158c8683e65352c3ea14fb5c6c95f8b6f3b0f4309</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">5280faf997ec1bb32a7160d02c323a9a203a75e0cfccceb64cd8b481810b7aa4</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-research-1} shows where the ledger enters execution. The authorized contract constrains deterministic workflow code; the model contributes subtask content and uses only the permitted tools. The right-hand ``verified result'' denotes an output checked within that scope, not authorization to change the contract or release the service. Behavioral examples must supply the expectations against which such an output is judged.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04-from-a-request-to-a-versioned-intention-ledger</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06076" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:11">
      <data key="k523">x06076</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">31d5a95b7efee7b1f7427ad193ba84c1073f94aaab7d7af9d27f50367edf6f59</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">5280faf997ec1bb32a7160d02c323a9a203a75e0cfccceb64cd8b481810b7aa4</data>
      <data key="k600">Hassan\textquotesingle s roadmap \autocite{W152} and research on rejected agent PRs \autocite{W071} motivate coordination and review without establishing an optimal gate sequence. Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-research-2} makes our proposed sequence explicit: validate the authorized delta before asking the model for a new patch, then rerun the affected contracts and independent checks. The dashed return brings unresolved evidence back to the control layer; it does not let the model silently rewrite intention. This keeps a late requirement small enough to trace without regenerating the entire system.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04-a-delta-driven-iterative-brownfield-lifecycle</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06077" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:12">
      <data key="k523">x06077</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch04-invalidation-loop</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">a80039c8696e1dd4b0b4a79179f3e141495a22d9984583888a21bf6b7f128412</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked04.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d2c109d282dc74603d2072cf2de3ffd75db3b2859a785600f00ee7ad98eb421e</data>
      <data key="k600">The return arrow in Figure~\ref{fig:ch04-invalidation-loop} starts another impact analysis after the next delta is authorized; it does not reopen every invariant. For the change in the table, invalidate the Treasury boundary fixture and its new-decision tests, while retaining replay, audit, cross-border and high-risk obligations. The checker derives expected behavior from INT-002, not from the maker's patch. Exercise~\ref{ex:ch04} asks you to author this change ledger. Research-versus-proposal distinctions are in Appendix~\ref{app:methodology}, \S\ref{app:commentary-ch04}.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch04:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06078" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:13">
      <data key="k523">x06078</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch05-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">7706b54a97c030fd16787f3953e3463af9f3bfa831eae52f48c243e2b5885f1a</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">76344b570df88cc78f651c5b435916b41ff1ecfb56d0133e1f08bb5b028e801e</data>
      <data key="k600">Before adopting a headline number, inspect the numerator and denominator: warnings per function or per thousand lines, code samples or accepted patches, total findings or high-severity findings, generated candidates or deployed changes. A matched sample can still be biased if a docstring omits the surrounding repository\textquotesingle s constraints. Conversely, an observational comparison of merged pull requests may exclude failed proposals and hide review effort. The engineering lesson is to match the study design to the question, then preserve its limitations in the citation. Read Figure~\ref{fig:ch05-research-1} in that order: corpus selection, enrichment, measurement and validation determine what a quality claim can mean. Its final box concerns statistical and sensitivity checks on the analysis, not certification that the merged software is safe in production.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch05-reading-ai-versus-human-studies-correctly</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06079" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:14">
      <data key="k523">x06079</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch05-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">13e3bf068c852a38af6e80d17d55ee06ae76b27e1319b76c13020b9ccfbffacc</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter05.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">76344b570df88cc78f651c5b435916b41ff1ecfb56d0133e1f08bb5b028e801e</data>
      <data key="k600">A separate comparison, summarized in Figure~\ref{fig:ch05-research-2}, groups repositories by prior AI-tool exposure. Its velocity row differs between the agent-first and IDE-first cohorts, while both show worsened maintainability signals in the summarized estimates. The aligned boxes compare directions, not equal effect sizes. For our service, the lesson is to track later change effort alongside immediate output rather than let a velocity gain stand in for maintainability.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch05-post-merge-evolution-and-maintenance-burden</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06080" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:15">
      <data key="k523">x06080</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch06-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">be01d6c2ea166e8f5c23365438e8be5bdc883d213a7690527adb5faf8e2a6ffc</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c0e22a9113e0fd8bfc4f632c25df153a2756fcb3bf726534a5713a93ece6fa2</data>
      <data key="k600">The critical transition in Figure~\ref{fig:ch06-research-1} is from a suggested name to an installed artifact: a name becoming available in a registry does not establish its trustworthiness. The control beneath the path therefore combines existence checks with provenance and locked dependencies. Our proposed gate requires approved identity and version review before installation, including for tool servers and skills. Pinning limits ambiguity but does not establish integrity. The teaching laboratory checks only a local manifest; it does not resolve or install packages over the network.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch06-dependency-provenance-and-hallucinated-packages</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06081" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:16">
      <data key="k523">x06081</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch06-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">3f78cc4849524089d8ee791fbf9b6bbdb2ce323d02e5648f14fe7cb659341edd</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter06.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c0e22a9113e0fd8bfc4f632c25df153a2756fcb3bf726534a5713a93ece6fa2</data>
      <data key="k600">Our proposed profile uses explicit tool operations, no wildcard shell grants, no default network egress, pinned tool declarations and structured audit logs. Skills and servers are reviewed like other executable dependencies; a friendly description is not an authorization. The laboratory rejects a manifest containing a floating tool version or broad shell permission and accepts a narrowly scoped manifest. It does not execute or authenticate any remote MCP server. The fork in Figure~\ref{fig:ch06-research-2} places enforcement after interpretation: even when the model accepts an instruction from a repository file, the runtime must separately allow the operation or deny its side effect. Reading content and acquiring authority remain distinct events.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch06-harness-configuration-skills-and-external-services</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06082" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:17">
      <data key="k523">x06082</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">12b8c6b6ca538821919bfd1c9f3a6b882e99403d83476af691041b0fd3d5897f</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">1bbb5af2473938ef0cee310a060ecc9a00673ed6daaff11af94ce508d4defcee</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-research-1} makes the conditioning in \autocite{W079} important: the bars compare how often two models choose the same wrong answer \emph{given that both are wrong}. They do not show how often the models fail overall. Agreement above the uniform wrong-choice baseline warns against treating consensus as independent evidence. Together with evaluator self-preference in broader LLM judgments \autocite{W082}, it motivates diversifying evidence sources; its quantitative transfer to software defect detection remains unverified.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07-independent-checkers-and-correlated-error</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06083" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:18">
      <data key="k523">x06083</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">640454a5b25b369e6987867b3193dc4615ca7c931fc1aef66bd43af80253cdab</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">1bbb5af2473938ef0cee310a060ecc9a00673ed6daaff11af94ce508d4defcee</data>
      <data key="k600">Every attempt retains a task identifier, code hash, tool version, diff, tests, failure reason, time or cost budget and resulting state. \autocite{W101}, \autocite{W095} and \autocite{W151} motivate caution about self-review and policy separation, but do not validate this exact retry policy. The steps in Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-research-2} represent distinct obligations: establish scope and contract, test behavior, review the evidence, and decide on release. Passing the test-oracle step does not satisfy the neighboring obligations. The staircase is a checklist of evidence boundaries, not a calibrated rise in reliability.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07-bounded-repair-versus-independent-acceptance</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06084" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:19">
      <data key="k523">x06084</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch07-independent-oracle</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">39133958ed6af4dc0bcbad476377880b1273fad5290d9063e78efb1b2ed17284</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">didactics/worked07.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">9e9e6ba0730240be5f7e150066b86a6efb15bd5375f7e17daf7b38c818cc6d00</data>
      <data key="k600">Suppose a maker changes the Treasury ceiling to EUR~3,000 and writes a test that computes its expected result using the very same function under test. The test can pass even if the function ignores the ceiling entirely. The checker must instead receive expected outcomes from an independently approved contract and an external test harness. The two branches in Figure~\ref{fig:ch07-independent-oracle} start from the same authorized contract, rather than deriving the expected answer from the candidate. They converge at the reviewer so that implementation and independently specified expectations can be compared. A second actor alone would not provide that independence.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch07:worked-example</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06085" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:20">
      <data key="k523">x06085</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch08-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">c406a6173946c91483fc24466d0f397111e3d012eeb9014be76e14526fdc63c4</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d3c4f31ca0fde0db8524e4a533adf2001c1488aadddf564cc5b3c37c8c585666</data>
      <data key="k600">Xiang et al.~\autocite{W102} give a particularly useful verification-cost counterexample. On 116 complete-case LiveCodeBench problems, review by Claude changes Codex passing outputs from 83 to 104 (+21), at \$0.443 versus \$0.190 per task; the opposite reviewer ordering lowers Claude's successes from 106 to 96 while increasing modeled inference cost from \$0.226 to \$0.382 per task. Table~2 provides numerator and denominator for independent \emph{percentage arithmetic}, and Table~4 provides discordances for exact McNemar test rechecks. Neither calculation replays the model calls, proves transfer to repository review, or guarantees a cost-effective production policy. A reviewer remains accountable for independent oracles, acceptance and regression risk. Figure~\ref{fig:ch08-research-1} decomposes those net changes into failures fixed and previously passing answers broken. Read each two-letter label as writer then reviewer: the green and red bars must be considered together. More corrections can coexist with regressions, so a review policy needs both counts rather than a tally of helpful comments.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch08-self-review-cross-model-review-and-shared-blind-spots</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06086" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:21">
      <data key="k523">x06086</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch08-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">4f5c742427d0f633b73efc1a0859a1a2450db48d0aef3e221190c6cadab82c2d</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter08.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d3c4f31ca0fde0db8524e4a533adf2001c1488aadddf564cc5b3c37c8c585666</data>
      <data key="k600">Cost adds another dimension in Figure~\ref{fig:ch08-research-2}. Each arrow begins at a writer-only baseline; moving right means greater inference cost, while moving up or down means a higher or lower pass rate. The almost horizontal A-to-AA route buys little net change in this sample, and the downward A-to-AO route spends more while losing passes. These are task-level comparisons, not a production cost model, but they expose why an additional review step must earn its place.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch08-self-review-cross-model-review-and-shared-blind-spots</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06087" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:22">
      <data key="k523">x06087</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch09-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">70438904f7aa46d1ba1bd684d2d8b157c9304619340e22fadb749359c7fa3288</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d0d7b46ec9ac8c80f5d51df8f0b25b83bf89ced3daa1eb6c8de701ecbf7dc610</data>
      <data key="k600">The package must record omissions. Finding one threshold constant does not prove there are no other consumers. An old passing test does not prove the current branch passes. A model-generated meeting summary is not an approved contract. Missing facts that affect acceptance should produce questions for the relevant owner, not confident guesses. The branching in Figure~\ref{fig:ch09-research-1} separates a recorded event from the semantic claim drawn from it before retrieval joins them again. Its ``what is true'' label must be read as a version-scoped assertion: observing a v1 decision does not establish the rule for a new v2 request.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch09-context-assembly-for-an-agent</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06088" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:23">
      <data key="k523">x06088</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch09-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">be0a5b5d392e447bf979c79064fc5ddc2de175ef2c0cdf814041fd4a24b543a2</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">d0d7b46ec9ac8c80f5d51df8f0b25b83bf89ced3daa1eb6c8de701ecbf7dc610</data>
      <data key="k600">INT-002 invalidates Treasury boundary expectations for new decisions and the current policy-fixture reference. It does not invalidate the high-risk invariant, the OPS threshold or historical idempotency decisions. A graph dependency walk can identify candidate impacts, but a human reviewer must challenge missing edges. The memory system should preserve historical evidence and explicitly identify which checks need rerunning. Figure~\ref{fig:ch09-research-2} addresses a different failure: losing required state during compaction or reset. Typed records pass through a validated writeback journal before durable storage; the lower box requires stopping when that preservation cannot be guaranteed. Preserving a record intact still does not make its contents current or authorized.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch09-memory-consistency-decay-and-invalidation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06089" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:24">
      <data key="k523">x06089</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch10-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">a84a799c02c8ac283917097c4d2b7d2f59d9d52487414e087b89e132871555a4</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">c9de72e9b9cbeeb7a7ab5044994f1de717789bd9e443b6e0e694e6b108ba81e4</data>
      <data key="k600">Following the expert-to-tour-to-learner path in Figure~\ref{fig:ch10-research-1}, a maintainer can curate three stops through the service. First inspect INT-001 and INT-002 and predict the EUR~4,000 Treasury outcome under each revision. Then trace \texttt{ApprovalService.evaluate} and explain why replay does not use the current ceiling. Finally inspect the defective legacy route and identify a contract-derived counterexample to its HIGH-risk behavior. The lower strip turns the tour into a proposed check of independent reasoning: explain an invariant, predict a failure and make an unaided change. Completing the tour is preparation for that check, not proof of durable learning.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch10-learning-through-explanations-repairs-and-code-tours</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06090" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:25">
      <data key="k523">x06090</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch10-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">2</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">66cd0db2d86908b07a1673f1eeebbd583728e249fc7e7fa50f5300dc02ce2cc4</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter10.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">c9de72e9b9cbeeb7a7ab5044994f1de717789bd9e443b6e0e694e6b108ba81e4</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch10-research-2} helps separate those outcomes. Its arrow leads from assisted work to an \emph{immediate} unaided quiz, not to a delayed retention measurement. The lower strip describes observed patterns of engagement, not randomly assigned teaching strategies. A mentoring programme can therefore use these observations to frame questions, but needs its own later transfer assessment before claiming that assisted practice produced lasting competence.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch10-mentoring-and-apprenticeship-in-a-team-with-agents</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06091" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:26">
      <data key="k523">x06091</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch11-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">1223702a42063d438c983d72a1d0be637250d5713ebdfd7508f43ed2a8db032f</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter11.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c3012ea9fe30a0ad57c8abb5c046a010f02ea71f46042e2cdf2c6aee47fac90</data>
      <data key="k600">Read the dot matrix in Figure~\ref{fig:ch11-research-1} across each row: filled dots mark provisions appearing together, and the right-hand count belongs to that selected combination. The rows illustrate how rules on contributions can coexist with requirements for human involvement, disclosure and accountability. They are neither a complete sample total nor a recommended policy ranking. For the service, define each obligation explicitly and evaluate the resulting review burden, acceptance quality and unwanted workarounds.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch11-policies-that-make-expectations-visible</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06092" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:27">
      <data key="k523">x06092</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch11-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">befbbaef788ed066d7a0cce32742aec03d7e30fb4bc6257725052a4362129840</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter11.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">2c3012ea9fe30a0ad57c8abb5c046a010f02ea71f46042e2cdf2c6aee47fac90</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch11-research-2} shows why those controls need a channel-specific scope. The upper bar classifies policies on code contributions; the lower bars record an absence of explicit guidance for communication and issues or security. Silence in a policy is not permission for an agent to post externally or disclose sensitive information. Our gate profile must state these boundaries separately rather than inherit them from a general allowance to submit code.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch11-executable-policy-as-an-engineering-proposal</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06093" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:28">
      <data key="k523">x06093</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch12-research-1</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">5f8c0818a87b7b35e479181b8e9bfed0cba3f9653cb849fd6d099013a4b6bf58</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">dbf4854f748601e0dd7778f39625870b36752dac82df792108a48d1b62cc701f</data>
      <data key="k600">The queue in Chapter~\ref{chap:11} gives a local reading of Figure~\ref{fig:ch12-research-1}. Candidate generation feeds review and integration, while the dashed capacity boundary reminds us that downstream delivery can remain constrained. More upstream work then accumulates instead of becoming proportionally more releases. The economic question is whether the intervention expands capacity at the constrained stage or reduces the evidence-gathering effort required there; faster generation alone answers neither.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch12-why-cheap-generation-may-increase-total-cost</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06094" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:29">
      <data key="k523">x06094</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:ch12-research-2</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">60460ac8a1e8eaeb5280e3b165572753501420b4b7b316aeac236285510d09de</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">chapters/chapter12.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">dbf4854f748601e0dd7778f39625870b36752dac82df792108a48d1b62cc701f</data>
      <data key="k600">Figure~\ref{fig:ch12-research-2} places the long-term question on a skill axis. The two curves represent stylized cohorts, and the vertical line marks the model's active-expert threshold $a_t$; neither their relative heights nor their displacement estimates our team's future headcount or competence. The diagram asks how access to expertise changes what a later cohort can learn. Training time, attrition, supervision and delayed competence therefore belong in the investment discussion, but require longitudinal observations rather than numbers read from these illustrative curves.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">ch12-the-apprenticeship-and-long-term-skill-economy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06095" source="EDITION:WOP:READER:V9:20261011" target="JPG:V7:30">
      <data key="k523">x06095</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"v9_reading_passage"</data>
      <data key="k561">fig:app-evidence-to-teaching</data>
      <data key="k563">1</data>
      <data key="k570">Current reader-prose linkage only</data>
      <data key="k577">1</data>
      <data key="k592">bc16e9628d8feb824301ec24cecad3f654f1573c3e72365ad060a095f3fa3385</data>
      <data key="k596">READER_REVISION_V9</data>
      <data key="k598">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
      <data key="k599">71c69a94ecdbaa12b7170f8d564bb34bb1af99a9a0a23766dc28687589743093</data>
      <data key="k600">A useful evidence trail names the publication and version, locates the relevant passage, states a bounded claim and explains how that claim informs a decision. Figure~\ref{fig:app-evidence-to-teaching} follows that route. Read across its upper row from publication to claim to engineering interpretation. The lower branch carries the source's qualifications into the example, so that the practical lesson does not quietly acquire more authority than the evidence supplies.</data>
      <data key="k603">FIGURE_EXPLAINED_IN_READER_PROSE_V9</data>
      <data key="k610">app:graph-construction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="x06096" source="V03" target="V02">
      <data key="k523">x06096</data>
      <data key="k524">provenance</data>
      <data key="k525">"ND-e3d5306483368531"</data>
      <data key="k545">EDITORIAL_CONTENT_COMPARISON_NOT_INDEPENDENT_CORROBORATION</data>
      <data key="k560">EDITORIAL_NOT_EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION</data>
      <data key="k596">ND.zip; editorial file-level mapping, 2026-10-11</data>
      <data key="k597">La directory e il titolo forniti dall’autore identificano la seconda edizione dello stesso volume; non è una seconda fonte empirica indipendente.</data>
      <data key="k603">ND_SECOND_EDITION_OF</data>
      <data key="k615">ND/AI_SDD_ENG_V2</data>
      <data key="k617">0</data>
