      <data key="k597">Proposizione del file: L’unità economica diventa l’esito verificato, non il token economico o la velocità del singolo contributore. Confronto (cost): Confrontare il costo dell’intero esito accettato, inclusi verifica e rilavorazione; ROI di scenario e testimonianze di consumo non sono rendimenti sperimentali. Scheda P095: A follow-up analysis of the 2026 reader survey examines tool costs, usage limits, developer identity and uneven changes to engineering work.</data>
      <data key="k603">ND_EDITORIAL_COMPARISON</data>
      <data key="k614">Introduction: From Cheap Assistance to Variable-Cost Production (L12); The Cost Structure of a Loop (L107); Context accumulation and execution cost (L115)</data>
      <data key="k615">NDLE/new_chapters/chapter03_economics.tex</data>
      <data key="k617">12</data>
      <data key="k627">Frozen v6 node P095 summary/contribution and limitation</data>
      <data key="k628">Uses the same respondent cohort as AI Tooling 2026 and key trends Part 2; not independent replication. Builders, shippers and coasters are interpretive response groupings, not a validated psychological or competency typology. The author reports 906 responses for the shared 2026 cohort. This is not an independently counted sample; comparisons with other survey waves are not a matched longitudinal panel. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
      <data key="k631">NO</data>
    </edge>
